{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts","id":1318724,"title":"At the Throne of Chaos: Nocturnal 3e [Brainstorming/Thoughts]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-15T11:55:00-07:00","id":1318724,"title":"At the Throne of Chaos: Nocturnal 3e [Brainstorming/Thoughts]","content":"While I am aware that waiting to at least the Storyteller's Guide in order to see how Getimians turn up is, probably, the wisest move, as an ardent Nocturnals fan I'm kinda of tired of waiting and living in a constant waiting and fear that my favorite Exalted splat would be invalidated. As such, I thought that while we don't know exactly about the capabilities of the Getimians, we probably know enough to start and developing the core themes of what being a Nocturnal means- or, at least, what is the base upon which we could be building in order to make the Nocturnals into something unique.<br /> <br /> First, we should examine what we actually know about the Getimians-<br /> <br /> a) Each of them is a stillborn fate, a person who should not have existed, yet does<br /> b) Whatever their maker and &quot;god&quot; may be, Rakan Thulio is the most dominant figure in their early life, contacting them through dreams and visions to lure them to his cause<br /> c) Getimians are known to host pattern spiders in their spine, which move through their body and shift the Essence between their chakras<br /> d) Their Essence is divided into yin and yang pools, with certain Charms working differently depending on the Essence which powers them<br /> e) Using a form of internal alchemy (called Getimian Alchemy), they can synthesize new Fates and unleash them upon the world from the yin/tang Essence<br /> f) They are created- not by Rakan Thulio, but they are more in the style of Alchemical/Liminal Exalted than the others by the virtue of not really being existing mortals which gained Exaltation, but entities which were born due to the event which formed their Exaltation<br /> g) have access to Sidereal Martial Arts (I think) and resonate with Starmetal<br /> <br /> Now, looking at what we know, I must say that they don't seem to have much in common with what I think about when I think about Nocturnals- but there may be some conceptual similarities. The biggest overlaps may come from the connection to the Sidereal Exalted, the possible paradox/time manipulation themes, and the possible mechanical similarity between Fluctuations and Getimian Alchemy.<br /> <br /> Now, the first overlap is also the easiest to solve- that is, the relationship between Sidereals and Nocturnals vs Sidereals and Getimians. To quote Vance, Nocturnals serve more as the Sidereals' Lunars, while the Getimians are their Abyssals/Infernals. While The Nocturnals have some... complicated relationships with the Chosen of the Maidens, the thing is that they share kinship- just like how Nox and his sisters had before the Primordial War. That is expressed in their themes- the Sidereals represents fate, order and maintenance of Creation. The Nocturnals represents free will, dreams and possibilities of the unknown. The Sidereals weave and maintains Creation's future, while the Nocturnals introduce change and possibilities upon which they could draw. They complement each other, just like how the Solars' shinning perfection and the Lunars' shifting forms challenge and complete one another to allow each of them to grow.<br /> <br /> The Getimians, on the other hand, don't seem to do that- theirs is an existence which should not be, and each carriers a seed of not a future which might be, but of a past which was erased, discarded and lost- or at least, thought to be lost, until perhaps &quot;found&quot; by Rakan Thulio. Getimians see Heaven and its messengers as their enemies (at least, at first), and feel no &quot;kinship&quot; to those who may be responsible to the life they should have had, yet were taken from them.<br /> <br /> The last overlap is also not that impossible to solve, as the themes and concepts behind the two mechanics seems to be different- Nocturnals use Fluctuations in order to produce their visions of what the future holds, transforming the world around them to produce new possibilities. Those possibilities are always presented as temporary creations- and what grants the Nocturnals their title as Heralds. They show what the world could produce- dreaming a world which does not exist, but might be. <br /> <br /> Getimian Alchemy is described somewhat differently- it is meant to allow the Getimian to control their own, personal fate, and unleash new fates upon the world. They carefully balance and control their internal energies in order to produce a new fate- one which goes against Fate's web. They don't imagine a different world and then make that dream into reality- they enforce their own will, their own fate, upon the Loom to disrupt it. It is even described differently- as the Getimians weave a new fate which either disrupts the patterns of the Loom or control the movement of their own fates, while the Nocturnals cause the Loom to shake and twist for only a short time, to shape the world to their needs.<br /> <br /> Now, the remaining overlap is the most difficult to estimate, as we don't know much about the extent of the Getimians' time manipulation abilities other than that their existence is, basically, an alternative timeline which does not exist and that their name has a connotation of &quot;time&quot; (even though the actual meaning is &quot;to happen&quot;. Well, that and that the Nox vs Grougaloragran battle from Wakfu could be used as an example for a Getimian vs Lunar fight. From the Nocturnal's side, the time manipulation is a derivative of their more general theme- that is, possibilities. Possibilities are, after all, possible futures. Choosing between alternative futures could be interpenetrated as choosing between different timelines. Choosing between different timelines is practically time travel. However, I think that it needs to be emphasized that Nocturnals should govern the <i>future</i>- what might be, not might have been.<br /> <br /> So, after talking so much about Nocturnals are already different than Getimians, we should ask what Nocturnals should be in 3e, and which of their themes should be emphasized. As this question was already asked <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1160492-nocturnals-fans-what-do-you-consider-iconic\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61600-nocutrnals-3e-looking-forward\">here</a>, we should first sum up those two and build upon them in our journey after the place of the Chosen of Possibilities in 3e-<br /> <br /> a) Fluctuations are, of course, important- the ability to call forth a new possibility is the iconic power of those Exalts. As such, we need to make sure that Fluctuations are both mechanically compelling and setting-wise unique, and that they truly express the idea of a &quot;future which might be&quot;.<br /> <br /> b) Alter Ego is yet another cool concept, as well as their renewal- dying and being born as a different person, or creating an ideal self, both express the themes of possibility and choice over fate. The Getimian work to enforce themselves upon the world, while the Nocturnal shape themselves toward a future only they can see.<br /> <br /> c) Probability and paradox, re-defining what is possible and what the future holds. Practically, both cheating your way out of a situation and solving a paradox by re-defining the problem. Kind of reminding how Nocturnal Exaltations were originally trapped- as Nox is the god of possibilities, his Essence was captured by an impossible situation- and creating a way out of that paradox was the only way to free the Exaltations. Nocturnals are cheaters, who find loopholes in the rules of the universe in order to make the impossible, possible.<br /> <br /> d) References to quantum mechanics have been emphasized many times through the original book- which makes sense. Quantum mechanics is a probabilistic theory, which defines that you can't know what the future holds. More specifically, the game leaned toward the Many Worlds Interpretation, and the Nocturnals choosing which future they would live in. As 3e leans more toward a fantasy styling of the setting and less magi-tech one, perhaps the references should be adjusted or toned down.<br /> <br /> e) Adjustments for the Curse of Servitude may be required, for both mechanical and setting-wise reasons. It may have been seen as too limiting, and its story may reinforce the theme of &quot;Sidereals are at fault of everything which is wrong about the world&quot;. Still, I think its existence is required to make sure that the Nocturnals are, indeed, harlequins and cheaters, and gives an anchor to their conflict for freedom. I kinda toyed with the thought of modifying the curse into the inert nature of Nox- the god which could not choose between sides, and tried to choose both, and making the Curse being tied to their intimacies- that is, the stronger they care about someone (either positively or negatively), the more that someone has power over the Nocturnals, physically making them into &quot;slaves to their passions&quot;, just like their god.<br /> <br /> f) Magical materials- while it was Adamant in 2e, as it meant to cover the &quot;missing Exalted&quot; situation, in 3e it was confirmed that the Heart Eater were originally those Exalts. As such, another material may be needed- Onyx was suggested, but we already have two &quot;stoney&quot; materials (jade and adamant), and &quot;magical onyx&quot; does not strike me as having too much of a mythical connections. Perhaps using some metals with alchemical significance could be better- magical copper is painfully missing in the setting, and Black Lead was eventually not used as the Infernals' magical material (at least, in 2e). Perhaps the Nocturnals don't have a resonating magical material at all- they simply can't favor one material over the others, and limit themselves in the process.<br /> <br /> g) Another thing to consider is that 3e explicitly tries to not tell us why exactly someone gains an Exaltation, and as such saying that the Nocturnals are chosen among those with &quot;thwart fates&quot; could be against its themes. Still, I think that it should kept in some fashion, as it signifies that Nocturnals work toward a future not dictated by fate. Perhaps the Exaltation would take the form of who they may be, as Nox takes their own faces to offer them a freedom outside of fate's web?<br /> <br /> h) Finally, some choices need to be made about Nox himself. As a god of possibilities, I won't be surprised if there would be as many myths about his origin as his chosen- was a he betrayer god, siding with the Primordials over his kin? Was he betrayed, his sisters not trusting his unpredictable nature? Is he an Incrana at all? Is he an entity from the future, trying to pave the possibility for its own existence? Or perhaps a being from the past, whose existence was removed being recognition? Does he creates paradoxes, or perhaps tries to solve them? Is the act of Exaltation is perhaps granting his Chosen the future that they yearn for, and the power to achieve it? Does Nox exists at all, or is he simply a title used by the future self of each and every one of us?<br /> <br /> Well, that's it for the sum up- and I think it is enough material to, at least, start to conceptually build the place for Nocturnals in 3e's setting. Please feel free to share your thoughts on the subject!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T13:38:23-07:00","id":1318736,"title":"","content":"I definitely think Nocturnals and Getimians can be distinct enough that you can have both, but yeah at present its easier to think their to similar, we really need the anima banners of Getimians lol. That said I think Nocturnals are a solid enough concept that would benefit a conversion, though I have some opinions, ideas, and critiques.<br /> <br /> 1) For the Magic Materials, I would suggest doing something along the Liminal then just add another one straight up. I have a couple of reasons for this. One, just adding a new magical material feels a bit cheap. Even with adamant being a secret one, its ultimately something which has been constant. Plus you can argue how exactly would the Essence of Nox would have been able to interact with Creation to create a metal while he's stuck in the Loom. plus the new origin for star metal fits to much with his domain that I can see it being probable. Two, as is Nox relationship with the Night Sky which houses the stars could be a perfect enough explanation of why his Chosen would have it as Neutral but not Resonant. Nox is not the stars after all, he holds them up, he touches them, hangs them. His darkness may hold infinite possibilities for new stars but he is not the god of stars, thus keeping it connected but distant. Also probably should not have the firmament made of adamant, and instead be vague what is. After all the Daystar is gone. From what we know the Sun is just the Sun, thus the Night sky could just be empty space, space that could be anything though. As Nox is Infinite Possibilities<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the same logic then they should also be neutral to Moonsilver, which honestly I wouldn't mind<br /> <br /> 2) I certainly agree with a changing of the Curse of Servitude, and on to that. Nox's and the Nocturnals fluff should probably be taken a good revision. With how it is written out it there are some points that don't really fit with how 3e handles things, like to much information on the explanations. 3e tries to add mystery back into the setting and well if we don't do that to one of the mysterious gods then why would we? Like for one thing, the Incarnae no longer tinkers around with their Exaltations as it was previously. Sol and Luna being the ones responsible for the Color-Lunar Bond is gone. Thus its probably imperative to examine what exactly is Nox as an Incarnae? Its probably find to detail his original role, assisting the Maiden's in tending the Loom. You should mention Nox's nature in flux, how he was the brother of the Maidens and how while they planned destiny it was from him that all ideas sprung forth. But you should keep what happen to him as you said a mystery. Did he betray or was betrayed? One point I want to keep is that he is in the Loom, just keep how he got their unknown. Like did the Maiden's put him their, the Primordials, or was he always in it, being the structure that fate rests on, the threads of destinies being pulled from his body of possibilities. I think by keeping his nature unknown helps in keeping the antagonism between Sidereals and Nocturnals low. It is the Getimian's now that wants to disrupt fate, thinking that it is unfair and cruel. While Nocturnals should have some impetus in freeing Nox, it shouldn't be their end goal. Just one of many possibilities. Nocturnals should be able to stand at the middle line. Whether to support fate or destroy it. Another thing I want some insight on is some of the optional incarna that will be in Exigents. The patron of Umbrals, was also a traitor Incarna and frankly they sound similar to Nox so I want to examine it. Though they do seem to have different themes and will be non canon just like Nox, frankly I want to see how they are a traitor, how Nox is different and capitalize on it. In anywise fresh looks on the backstory and how Heralds and Harlequins work is probably good to do. Though note that a good point to think about that every Exalted that warred against and killed those that would become Neverborn is under the Great Curse. So if Harlequins fought in the war but was already under the Curse of Servitude and shackled with another curse, thats to much. So you idea for the Curse to be more on Nox's flux should go to the Heralds that are unbound while Harlequins should just have a Limit Track and their versions of breaks. Of course then you should look into why they fought for the Exalted Host if their not bound, what made them fight? Why are they different from Heralds?<br /> <br /> 3) Another thing that probably should be looked at is the Nature of Nocturnal Exaltation which you commented on. To be honest, destined for greatness interrupted by others doesn't sound to appealing to me. I'm fine with second chances but I think it should be laid down in an appealing matter that should fit in lie with Nox's theme of flux. Which probably should be clarified to be distinct from Luna's ever changing nature I guess. Also take away being Chosen from the greater good, yeah no by by. An Exaltation shouldn't come into morality, you shouldn't be automatically the good guys. Its you the players that make that decision. An Exaltation should give some insights to the patrons presences, themes, and personality. Even Dragon-Blooded who Exaltation is different all have some emotions and feelings that they Exalt to, something far grandeur then just simple. I also want to know exactly what is a stillborn fate that the Getimians have, and how that structures things to make it clear difference between them and Nocturnals who could be chosen for a &quot;Possible future&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> Well in any case, thats just a few of my thoughts anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-15-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T22:36:35-07:00","id":1318804,"title":"","content":"Here's a concept for a possible Nox origin that ditches the entire betrayed-and-shoved-into-a-loom thing :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nox was one of the very first beings created by the Primordials when they made Creation, the backdrop upon which the stars would take hold to then oversee the rest of Creation. He was a counterpart to the Voice in the Trench - where the Voice created things, he created times and circumstances for those things to appear in.<br /> <br /> Nox was a test prototype for Incarnae, and as such he falls somewhere in between the incomprehensible nature of the Primordials and the very human natures of the Incarnae. Rather than being simply a humanoid embodiment ruling over an aspect of the sky, he is both the literal night sky and a humanoid Incarnae ruling over it at the same time, somehow both the ruler and the domain.<br /> <br /> The primordial influence in his nature means that Nox's mind works in alien ways at the best of times. He was always strangely mad and didn't need to get shoved inside the Loom of Fate for that. He is apart from the other Incarnae not because his loyalties are dubious but because they are impossible to acquire in the first place. His stance in the primordial war was neutral, not as a moral stance or as a calculated move, but simply because taking a side would have narrowed down his own set of possible futures significantly, which was something he could not stand for.<br /> <br /> When the Incarnae created Exalted in their bid to overthrow the Primordials, Nox did not care for joining in the war but he was fascinated by the concept of beings who could resist the yoke of fate and by the possibilities they created. Therefore, he set about to create his own Exalted.<br /> <br /> It was a complete surprise for the Exalted host when Nocturnals appeared before them for the first time, offering to join their cause. But the joy of newfound allies became bittersweet when they realized many other Nocturnals had joined the Primordials instead. In the end, the dying Primordials did not distinguish friend from foe and struck all Nocturnals with the Great Curse. </div> </div> </div>For Exaltation :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nox selects his Chosen not out of any virtue or merit they have as individuals, but for their potential to create new possibilities. Looking through all possible futures, Nox takes notice of a mortal whom, if they just got a slight nudge in the right direction, could impact fate and possibilities in new and interesting ways, be they good or bad. If this piques his interest, he will grant that mortal Exaltation at the very moment where it would give them an opportunity to radically change the course their destiny, creating long-ranging tremors in the Loom of Fate.<br /> <br /> Nox created his Chosen with the hope that they would surprise even him with the new possibilities they brought with them. He never tells them what to do, but he is known to offer them cryptic hints into ways they might create many new possible futures with their actions. More experienced Nocturnals know not to blindly follow his suggestions, as Nox does not care whether the outcome is positive or negative, just that it is new and unexpected. </div> </div> </div>For magical materials :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nocturnals are Neutral with Starmetal, Moonsilver and Adamant, and Dissonant with all other materials. A Nocturnal may enhance her connection with her artifact by using it to create new possibilities. When a Nocturnal uses her Artifact in a dramatic way that creates a new possibility which could not have existed without this specific artifact, she may increase her resonance with the Artifact by 1 level for the Scene, making Starmetal, Moonsilver and Adamant Resonant and all other materials Neutral. </div> </div> </div><i>Edit : Changed the concept for how/why Nocturnals were created after TheSarcasticSage pointed out my original concept didn't fit with 3E lore</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 06-16-2019, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T02:10:29-07:00","id":1318818,"title":"","content":"I remember Nocturnals fondly, and I'm interested in seeing what comes of this thread, but this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1318804#post1318804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even though Nox remained neutral in the conflict, Luna talked Autochton into creating Exalted for him despite the Maidens' objections. She based her argument on the conviction that these Exalted, gifted with more human natures, would have the necessary humanity to appreciate the effort to overthrow the Primordials and would willingly join the rebellion. And thus poetically the Nocturnal were created for the possible future they might bring and for their potential as free-willed agents. In the end not all Nocturnal joined the rebellion, but enough of them did for them to get hit by the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> Nox feels no kinship for his chosen nor any desire to rule over them, but he often interacts with them as they are his most potent tools for inserting new fates and possibilities into the world. The nature of these interactions are closer to the ravings of a mad hermit than that of a god overseeing his children.</div> </div> </div> </div>is not how things work in 3e. Autochton did not create any Exaltations but his own, and as per word of Dev, no one can make Exaltations for another. Also, every Exaltation is the choice of the God doing the exalting. There is no more automatic exalting in 3e. With the <i>possible</i> exception of the Dragon Blooded, and Alchemicals, every other Exalt is personally chosen by the entity granting the exaltation. Your patrons chose you, for what ever reason, and I think that creates better stories then the above idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T06:26:03-07:00","id":1318837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1318818#post1318818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Nocturnals fondly, and I'm interested in seeing what comes of this thread, but this:<br /> <br /> is not how things work in 3e. Autochton did not create any Exaltations but his own, and as per word of Dev, no one can make Exaltations for another. Also, every Exaltation is the choice of the God doing the exalting. There is no more automatic exalting in 3e. With the <i>possible</i> exception of the Dragon Blooded, and Alchemicals, every other Exalt is personally chosen by the entity granting the exaltation. Your patrons chose you, for what ever reason, and I think that creates better stories then the above idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the correction, I was unaware of that. I think I actually prefer this new way of handling it, so all the better.<br /> <br /> Here's a correction for the bit you quoted then :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Incarnae created Exalted in their bid to overthrow the Primordials, Nox did not care for joining in the war but he was fascinated by the concept of beings who could resist the yoke of fate and by the possibilities they created. Therefore, he set about to create his own Exalted.<br /> <br /> It was a complete surprise for the Exalted host when Nocturnals appeared before them for the first time, offering to join their cause. But the joy of newfound allies became bittersweet when they realized many other Nocturnals had joined the Primordials instead. In the end, the dying Primordials did not distinguish friend from foe and struck all Nocturnals with the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> Nox created his Chosen with the hope that they would surprise even him with the new possibilities they brought with them. He never tells them what to do, but he is known to offer them cryptic hints into ways they might create many new possible futures with their actions. More experienced Nocturnals know not to blindly follow his suggestions, as Nox does not care whether the outcome is positive or negative, just that it is new and unexpected. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:32:06-07:00","id":1318889,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Magical Materials: Actually, my initial thought was making them neutral toward all of existing materials, as a manifestation of Nox's inability to commit to a choice- from one side, they keep all options open. On the other, they can't really excel at anything. Perhaps they could, temporary, commit themselves to a certain MM, but they would have to give up something in exchange, becoming dissonant with another material. We should, of course, also decide how good the Nocturnals should be with Evocations- the guidelines say that the more that the Exalted wears its power on the outside, the less they can awaken Evocations from their weapon of choice. How external are the Nocturnals? Not so much, IMO, as they actually draw upon their imagination and vision for the future. Having them resonating with only Starmetal would also make them too similar in that respect to Sidereals and Getimians, and I think that three splats with the same MM choice is kinda boring. I agree on the concept of not forcing a new material unless it is called for, but I still wait to see my copper/lead/tin Exalts :P<br /> <br /> In short, my suggestion for the Nocturnals is having all materials as initially Neutral, with perhaps a way to commit themselves to one one the expense of the other. It reinforce their theme of possibilities and make them less predictable- something which Nox would probably like. If we do want to give a special place to a few materials, Epitome's suggestion does sounds good.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Curse- I was still working under the assumption that the Nocturnals have showed up after the Divine Rebellion. At any case, I think that some form of the Curse of Servitude would make the bet sense for them (as the Great Curse influence the passions of the Exalts, having them developing servitude toward their intimacies also makes a lot of sense). At any case, I wish to emphasis that the title Harlequins comes specifically due to their nature as &quot;bound servants&quot;. Harlequins, after all, come from the Commedia dell Arte, serving as the &quot;smart servant&quot; of the play which, from one side, was forced to serve their idiotic master, and from the other used their trickery and intelligence in order to defeat their master and allow the Lovers to unite. They are also clowns, of course- but their trickery comes from their servitude, and the same should be true for the Nocturnals, IMO. We should also consider the Sidereal- Nocturnal bond- in 3e, the Solar- Lunar bond is a deliberate creation of the Exalts themselves, as a form of political marriage, and a result of the Sunstrife Wars. As such, it would make me surprised if the Nocturnals would have exactly the same type of bond such as the Lunars. Perhaps the Nocturnal bond is more of a manifestation of their &quot;curse&quot;- Nox has strong kinship toward his sisters, be it love or hate. Usually, when a Nocturnal has a passion toward another individual, it is a one sided connection- but when it is formed toward a Sidereal, the curse &quot;resonates&quot;- and is nullified. Nocturnals are bond to everyone and everything they care about- except to the Chosen of the Stars. It is not a bond as much as of a lack of servitude, and for someone so riddled with connections, the lack of bond is more important from its existence, as for the Nocturnals, it grants them what they yearn for the most- true freedom. <br /> <br /> On the subject of Exaltation, having Nox himself choosing his Chosen does, of course, makes a lot of sense in 3e's setting. I'm still kind of a fan of Nox wearing the face of the possible future self of their Chosen, as it maintains the theme of time shenanigans and makes the Exaltation creepy- which I like. On Nox's origin, the reason that I think that having him a number of in-game origin stories which contradict each other is that it really works with his theme of possibilities- everything is true, as long as there is no evidence. Perhaps Nox actively tries to remove evidence for its existence, to make sure he won't be bound to a single possibility, and that he intentionally creates the many stories about his existence as a part of that process (which would really annoy his sisters). If Nox is still weaved into the Loom, I think that, like the Yozi's prison, freeing him should not be an option- just to make sure the game won't always evolve into &quot;freeing our god from the cruel web of fate&quot;. We should also consider the place of the Firmament in the setting, and when exactly the Nocturnals have showed up for the first time- as it would be the only constant event in all of Nox's contradicting stories. Were they in the Divine Revolution, fighting alongside their sibling Chosen? Or did they showed up only recently, coming with the Time of Tumult while speaking about a strange god which no one knows but the Maidens- and they aren't speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T12:40:10-07:00","id":1318924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1318889#post1318889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Curse- I was still working under the assumption that the Nocturnals have showed up after the Divine Rebellion. At any case, I think that some form of the Curse of Servitude would make the bet sense for them (as the Great Curse influence the passions of the Exalts, having them developing servitude toward their intimacies also makes a lot of sense). At any case, I wish to emphasis that the title Harlequins comes specifically due to their nature as &amp;quot;bound servants&amp;quot;. Harlequins, after all, come from the Commedia dell Arte, serving as the &amp;quot;smart servant&amp;quot; of the play which, from one side, was forced to serve their idiotic master, and from the other used their trickery and intelligence in order to defeat their master and allow the Lovers to unite. They are also clowns, of course- but their trickery comes from their servitude, and the same should be true for the Nocturnals, IMO. We should also consider the Sidereal- Nocturnal bond- in 3e, the Solar- Lunar bond is a deliberate creation of the Exalts themselves, as a form of political marriage, and a result of the Sunstrife Wars. As such, it would make me surprised if the Nocturnals would have exactly the same type of bond such as the Lunars. Perhaps the Nocturnal bond is more of a manifestation of their &amp;quot;curse&amp;quot;- Nox has strong kinship toward his sisters, be it love or hate. Usually, when a Nocturnal has a passion toward another individual, it is a one sided connection- but when it is formed toward a Sidereal, the curse &amp;quot;resonates&amp;quot;- and is nullified. Nocturnals are bond to everyone and everything they care about- except to the Chosen of the Stars. It is not a bond as much as of a lack of servitude, and for someone so riddled with connections, the lack of bond is more important from its existence, as for the Nocturnals, it grants them what they yearn for the most- true freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it,(and rereading the pdf, since it's been a while and I had the feeling i misremembered some stuff in my above post, which I did.). Being the cunning jesters is very much a part of the whole package. I have of ideas of how that could work, as I'm not personally inclined to the Curse of Subservience as is, where it gives penalties and denials from the commands of Celestials who could be other players, which might not go swell. Honestly those fit better as Limit Break analogies, which is basically the only time I'm comfortable taking away my players control. Rather they are always able to do whatever action they wish but like a Limit Track once you go against certain conditions(which can be like, all Harlequins have an Intimacy of obey Celestials, when they encounter one like how the Lunar Bond is) and accumulate enough limit then you are forced to certain roles, basically Limit as it is in nut shell. Though more options may present itself when the Sidereal Great Curse is detailed which is apparently different. At also another thing about the Subseverance. I would be up to expanding it so that Nocs wont just be under Celestials because well discounting Sids that's just Lunars and Solars. Opening them up to say Dragon-blooded could be interesting, like a Noc were to align themselves with a whole bloodline of Dragons and serves them for generations, with few being the wiser with how Noc renewal works. I think that opens up some stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the subject of Exaltation, having Nox himself choosing his Chosen does, of course, makes a lot of sense in 3e's setting. I'm still kind of a fan of Nox wearing the face of the possible future self of their Chosen, as it maintains the theme of time shenanigans and makes the Exaltation creepy- which I like. On Nox's origin, the reason that I think that having him a number of in-game origin stories which contradict each other is that it really works with his theme of possibilities- everything is true, as long as there is no evidence. Perhaps Nox actively tries to remove evidence for its existence, to make sure he won't be bound to a single possibility, and that he intentionally creates the many stories about his existence as a part of that process (which would really annoy his sisters). If Nox is still weaved into the Loom, I think that, like the Yozi's prison, freeing him should not be an option- just to make sure the game won't always evolve into &amp;quot;freeing our god from the cruel web of fate&amp;quot;. We should also consider the place of the Firmament in the setting, and when exactly the Nocturnals have showed up for the first time- as it would be the only constant event in all of Nox's contradicting stories. Were they in the Divine Revolution, fighting alongside their sibling Chosen? Or did they showed up only recently, coming with the Time of Tumult while speaking about a strange god which no one knows but the Maidens- and they aren't speaking. </div> </div> </div>As for Nocturnals shows up, my suggestion that instead of just having them being kept imprisoned. They are instead were released in the First Age which was the purpose of the Curse of Subservience. Because the Incarnae no longer has the thing of being fearful of their Chosen, instead of being more connected with them. An idea of how Nocturnals worked, was that in the various eras and kingdoms of the first age, now and again certain mysterious miracle workers would show up. They would be recognizable as Exalted, but the nature unknown and mysterious. They would find themselves under the reigns of the Exalted Host and use the powers to show their leiges futures that could be, possibilities of what might have been. They would disappear along with the fall of kingdoms, though they would also appear again in the ages to come. Smiling and continuing on the same. Becoming unassuming in the background despite their weird powers. Or that's one idea anyway. They aren't the viziers the Sidereals were, the spokesman of Heaven's wishes to the Host. But rather jesters and actors that showed the Host dreams and ideas of something different and fascinating. Or at least that's what first popped into my mind. I think an important difference is that the Nocturnals shouldn't be seen as antagonistic to the role of the Sidereals. But compliments and show something different. <br /> <br /> For the Firmament, not much good options there. Its basically the Nocturnals version of the Daystar and that's gone. Though on this topic if the Firmament becomes less of a thing there be a need to rerun the Empyrean Caste since their wouldn't be the Empyrean Wastes. I would be up to calling them Aethers if that happened, since that was a term used historically to talk about the space between stars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T07:13:13-07:00","id":1319043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1318924#post1318924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it,(and rereading the pdf, since it's been a while and I had the feeling i misremembered some stuff in my above post, which I did.). Being the cunning jesters is very much a part of the whole package. I have of ideas of how that could work, as I'm not personally inclined to the Curse of Subservience as is, where it gives penalties and denials from the commands of Celestials who could be other players, which might not go swell. Honestly those fit better as Limit Break analogies, which is basically the only time I'm comfortable taking away my players control. Rather they are always able to do whatever action they wish but like a Limit Track once you go against certain conditions(which can be like, all Harlequins have an Intimacy of obey Celestials, when they encounter one like how the Lunar Bond is) and accumulate enough limit then you are forced to certain roles, basically Limit as it is in nut shell. Though more options may present itself when the Sidereal Great Curse is detailed which is apparently different. At also another thing about the Subseverance. I would be up to expanding it so that Nocs wont just be under Celestials because well discounting Sids that's just Lunars and Solars. Opening them up to say Dragon-blooded could be interesting, like a Noc were to align themselves with a whole bloodline of Dragons and serves them for generations, with few being the wiser with how Noc renewal works. I think that opens up some stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood my suggestion- I didn't meant that the Curse would be that all Nocturnals have an intimacy toward Celestials. I meant that every Nocturnals would feel compelled to serve anyone (be it Celestial, Dragon Blooded, a god or even a regular mortal), toward which they have a strong intimacy- and stronger the intimacy, the more powerful the Curse. The only exception for this would be Sidereals, toward which they do not develop such a compulsion and are truly &quot;free&quot; with- some sort of a loophole in the Great Curse/Curse of Subservience that the Nocturnal Exalation <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the Firmament, not much good options there. Its basically the Nocturnals version of the Daystar and that's gone. Though on this topic if the Firmament becomes less of a thing there be a need to rerun the Empyrean Caste since their wouldn't be the Empyrean Wastes. I would be up to calling them Aethers if that happened, since that was a term used historically to talk about the space between stars. </div> </div> </div>I actually treat the Firmament as a new &quot;realm of existence&quot;, such as Yu Shan, the Underworld and Malfeas- it is the realm above, of strange mysteries and possible futures, instead of a physical representation of &quot;Nox&quot;. It would be a strange realm with strange beings, an abandoned wasteland of shattered stars and broken dreams. We could easily use it to make the setting more weird and mysterious, especially as, unlike the Daystar, it is a place- full with geography and denizens, instead of a weapon. In short, I think that unlike the Daystar and its like, the Firmament still has a place in 3e in its presentation of a different world.<br /> <br /> Also, it has just occurred to me that while we like to think about the Nocturnals as the &quot;quantum mechanics splat&quot;, in fact we could correspond each of the three &quot;fate manipulating&quot; splats to a certain quantum mechanics interpretation- Sidereals represents Bohemian Mechanics, where while the world seems random, all paths are already decided and fate is weaved, guiding individuals toward their pre-written story. Getimians are the Wavefunction Collapse, where during measurement whole universes are being erased from continuity, their information lost and existence removed. And Nocturnals are, of course, the Many Worlds interpretation, where all possibilities co-exist and flow next to each other, and it is only our limited minds which can grasp a single worldline instead of every possibility which was, is and will be.<br /> <br /> Just something to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T07:46:25-07:00","id":1319049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319043#post1319043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually treat the Firmament as a new &quot;realm of existence&quot;, such as Yu Shan, the Underworld and Malfeas- it is the realm above, of strange mysteries and possible futures, instead of a physical representation of &quot;Nox&quot;. It would be a strange realm with strange beings, an abandoned wasteland of shattered stars and broken dreams. We could easily use it to make the setting more weird and mysterious, especially as, unlike the Daystar, it is a place- full with geography and denizens, instead of a weapon. In short, I think that unlike the Daystar and its like, the Firmament still has a place in 3e in its presentation of a different world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. As a realm of existence, there could be a risk for the Firmament to overlap with the Wyld as The Weird Place, but maybe the Firmament is where time gets weird as opposed to the Wyld where matter gets weird. As to why it exists, maybe the Firmament act as a sort of Pole of Time, warding Creation from time aberrations that could slip in from the Wyld by trapping them like a net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T07:54:21-07:00","id":1319053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319043#post1319043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you misunderstood my suggestion- I didn't meant that the Curse would be that all Nocturnals have an intimacy toward Celestials. I meant that every Nocturnals would feel compelled to serve anyone (be it Celestial, Dragon Blooded, a god or even a regular mortal), toward which they have a strong intimacy- and stronger the intimacy, the more powerful the Curse. The only exception for this would be Sidereals, toward which they do not develop such a compulsion and are truly &amp;quot;free&amp;quot; with- some sort of a loophole in the Great Curse/Curse of Subservience that the Nocturnal Exalation</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I get you, I was just mostly commenting on how the Curse worked before, rather then on you suggestion. I'm just curious on exactly how that compulsion to work. Well the most easiest way is probably doing something with the social system though I haven't thought how yet though it's a start.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually treat the Firmament as a new &amp;quot;realm of existence&amp;quot;, such as Yu Shan, the Underworld and Malfeas- it is the realm above, of strange mysteries and possible futures, instead of a physical representation of &amp;quot;Nox&amp;quot;. It would be a strange realm with strange beings, an abandoned wasteland of shattered stars and broken dreams. We could easily use it to make the setting more weird and mysterious, especially as, unlike the Daystar, it is a place- full with geography and denizens, instead of a weapon. In short, I think that unlike the Daystar and its like, the Firmament still has a place in 3e in its presentation of a different world. </div> </div> </div>Making a new Realm would probably fit, I'm just worried to not take it as it was previously where it was literally Creation's Sky. With Stars being Towers and everything made of Adamant. Though from what suggesting I don't think you are saying that either which I'm fine with. Though theres a lot to keep figure out if that's the case but I prefer it like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T13:28:57-07:00","id":1319114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319053#post1319053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I get you, I was just mostly commenting on how the Curse worked before, rather then on you suggestion. I'm just curious on exactly how that compulsion to work. Well the most easiest way is probably doing something with the social system though I haven't thought how yet though it's a start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. My personal view is that having the Nocturnals bound to the will of other Celestials while Dragon Blooded are not part of it is something which should indeed go out of the window- it only serves as presenting Celestials as the &quot;bad guys&quot; and DBs as &quot;not true Exalts&quot;. Not to mention that with weird things such as Getimians, Liminals, Alchemicals and Exigents 9not to mention Hearteaters and their like), such a divide makes little to no sense in 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making a new Realm would probably fit, I'm just worried to not take it as it was previously where it was literally Creation's Sky. With Stars being Towers and everything made of Adamant. Though from what suggesting I don't think you are saying that either which I'm fine with. Though theres a lot to keep figure out if that's the case but I prefer it like this. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is a lot to figure out about Nocturnals in general in 3e, hence the thread :P (but seriously though, the Firmament was really popular among Nocturnal fans from what I could gather, so adapting it to the setting would be a good idea. Not to mention that theory that someone thought about in the forums that &quot;Across the Eight Directions&quot; could perhaps be treated as an in-setting expression, where will nowadays refers to the eight directions of Creation, it originally referred to an eight divine realms- Yu Shan, Malfeas, the Underworld, the Wyld and Autochtonia serving as few of those. The Firmament could be one of those. Just a random thought).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T13:31:14-07:00","id":1319115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319049#post1319049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that. As a realm of existence, there could be a risk for the Firmament to overlap with the Wyld as The Weird Place, but maybe the Firmament is where time gets weird as opposed to the Wyld where matter gets weird. As to why it exists, maybe the Firmament act as a sort of Pole of Time, warding Creation from time aberrations that could slip in from the Wyld by trapping them like a net.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds cool- while I will probably won't use the term &quot;Pole of Time&quot;, having it as a timeless place were relics and remains of the ruined past and future dreams is a nice beginning. We do have a trapped legion of the Balorain Crusade in there already, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T15:10:53-07:00","id":1319364,"title":"","content":"So a short sum up for what we need to work on for Nocturnal 3e update-<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter one: the Nocturnal Exalted-</b> would include the history of the Nocturnals and Nox, which may include a number of possible in setting versions, due to Nox serving as the God of Possibilities, as well as what is really known about the Chosen of the Night (which seems to be that they showed up somewhere during the early First Age, either before or after the Divine Revolution). It would also include the Nocturnal Exaltation in details- what the Chosen feels, sees and experience, and well as the unique features of Nocturnal Exaltation (like their interaction with their Curse, or the whispers of Nox, etc, etc).<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter two: Midnight Carnival</b>- a description of the Nocturnal society and their interactions with both each other and other Exalts. As the Nocturnals seems to be revised to show up during the First Age instead of being a modern phenomenon, they would have probably had enough time to develop society and such. If they are a modern creation, we should still consider their place in the world and ways they'll work with each other.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter three: Nebular Theaters</b>- for both Dragon- Blooded and Lunars there was a section about the civilizations based around the Exalts, and we know that Sijan would show up at either the Abyssal or Liminal books, which kinda makes me think that there should be a certain level of world building in splat books. However, the thing is that for Dragon Blooded, Lunars and Abyssals, such civilizations <i>makes sense</i> (the Realm as whole, Lunar Dominions and Shadowlands, correspondingly). In 2e, Nocturnals are not known to establish whole kingdoms around themselves. Perhaps that section should instead describe the Firmament? Or both a chapter for the Firmament and something about world-building, if there would be a really cool justification for why &quot;Nocturnal civilizations&quot; should exist, and how they would look like. Perhaps it could be a place to add some of the strange parallel worlds of Nox?<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter four: Character Creation</b>- exactly what the title says. It should be very simple, once we'll somehow solve all other issues.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter five: Traits</b>- new merits and flaws, such as the new adaption for &quot;Whispers&quot; (the ability to hear Nox), Castes (together with Anima effects and attributes), description of the Curse of Subservience and the &quot;Sidereal bond&quot; (however they would turn up), and perhaps any other special features of the Nocturnal Exaltation. Should the Nocturnals still have Paradox, or should it be replaced with something unique to them? I personally think that their Curse should be enough, but who knows. We should also refer to the tendency of Nox to hide the existence of his Chosen- are they still hard to remember and track down, or perhaps that feature should be revised as well? We should also decide about signature characters, but there are more urgent issues.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter six: Charms</b>- the themes of the Nocturnal Charms should be well solidified at this section. We should remember that they are best around attributes, and that Charms are not magical spells- but expression of the most basic and primal power of the Exaltation. That is, Charms are things that the Nocturnal can do, instead of secret techniques. Keywords should be assigned and decided in order to fully bring forth those themes. As their power level is that of a Celestial, they should be more or less comparable to Lunars/ Sidereals. <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter seven: Martial Arts and Sorcery</b>- we would probably need to work on some special Martial Arts styles which express the Nocturnal nature at its finest, as well as some spells and perhaps Initiations/ Shaping Rituals. Things which come from the Nocturnal culture and nature and express the best their role as Champions and the Night and Chosen of Possibilities, Heralds and Harlequins. We are still waiting for the rules for Necromancy, so no need to decide how well they know the dark arts- but their are probably able to reach Celestial Sorcery. While they are unable to learn Sidereal Martial Arts in 2e, should it still be the case in 3e? (I don't really think they should, but I would want to hear what others think).<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter eight: Forged From Night</b>- Evocations and artifacts, as well as deciding exactly how the Nocturnals work Evocations and if their have some affinity to some material or neutral to all, as well as if they have an ability to &quot;trick&quot; that affinity (see my and Epitome's suggestions about the subject).<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter nine: Wishes in the Dark</b>- Fluctuations and their capabilities in 3e.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter ten: Heralds and Harlequins</b>- example Nocturnal NPCs of importance in the Time of Tumult.<br /> <br /> Anything else we should add to the list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T15:58:37-07:00","id":1319370,"title":"","content":"A Storytelling chapter like there was in the 2E pdf could be very useful. It could discuss types of games you can run with Nocturnals Protagonists, present how to use them as Antagonists, suggest ways the ST can play out the bits of Lore that are left intentionally vague, and include information about the Manvantara and the 6th Caste in the event those things make the transition to 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T16:10:24-07:00","id":1319372,"title":"","content":"I think thats plenty enough for an outline. As for what its about.<br /> <br /> I to think that Noc's shouldn't have SMA, mainly as Attribute Exalts that would make them to broken, and frankly I don't want to make them to similar to Sids and Gets just because their connected to them. Though we still don't know why Gets are able to get SMA I don't see that as much justification for Nocturnals to get them. We will see. For the rest of the chapter, all of that will probably have to be created flat-out since I don't remember them getting any in the previous time by RO and co. So thats another thing that Exigents will be helpful with. <br /> <br /> Paradox, I don't know. For one thing I think having it makes it more likely for Sid vs Noc conflicts to happen, and I'm unsure whether that would be a good thing. And thats also something I think could probably be what Getimians is about but again I don't know. <br /> <br /> As for Civilizations, I don't think Nocturnals should get stuff as iconic as Lunar Dominions but that doesn't mean they shouldn't get anything. Creation is a big big place, much of it still empty. adding more shit won't hurt it much, well as long as it fits with the others, and I think it would be fun to see what type of factions develop among the Night's Chosen. How much would they be independent, and how many have found themselves under another Exalts command. I also think that if you are gonna include the Firmament that would be a good place to put it, how and why its a realm, whether it interacts with the rest like Yu Shan, what you can expect there and Caelain City, which would probably make a nice center of Nocturnal activity, as much as Great Forks is to Exigents. <br /> <br /> And lastly, talking about the Nocturnals Charm keywords, looking over on the pdf. One thing I can certainly say is that I think that got a bit to many so yeah they probably should be revised. Personally I think the one relating to Calibration is to specific to be practical, that and I think Nox shouldn't be made God of Calibration again. Mostly because I feel that should be Five Day's Darkness thing. I think that is fine as is. Or thats how I think anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T16:15:44-07:00","id":1319374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319370#post1319370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Storytelling chapter like there was in the 2E pdf could be very useful. It could discuss types of games you can run with Nocturnals Protagonists, present how to use them as Antagonists, suggest ways the ST can play out the bits of Lore that are left intentionally vague, and include information about the Manvantara and the 6th Caste in the event those things make the transition to 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes ST Chapter. Certainly would help a lot, forgot about it since the 3e cores no longer has them which is a bit impractical since they can be a help.<br /> <br /> Honestly I like Singularities and think they should stay, Manvantara though, not so much. I feel like its to complex of a concept that you should try to wrap your head around. Plus it was made to be a counterpart of Samsara, which I don't think is a thing in 3e anymore. Theirs probably easier ways of going about having Parallel World Caste and not trying to look of stuff that deeply","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T18:24:27-07:00","id":1319389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1318889#post1318889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Magical Materials: Actually, my initial thought was making them neutral toward all of existing materials, as a manifestation of Nox's inability to commit to a choice- from one side, they keep all options open.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the PC-creation level, making them neutral with everything effectively makes them worse than everybody else (except Liminals) with artifacts and Evocations. Sure, from a worldbuilding perspective they're better off than Sidereals and Getimians, since starmetal's rare and those two are dissonant with everything else. But when doing character creation, you just specify that the artifact you bought with your dots is of the material you're resonant with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1318889#post1318889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other, they can't really excel at anything. Perhaps they could, temporary, commit themselves to a certain MM, but they would have to give up something in exchange, becoming dissonant with another material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to choose a temporarily-resonant material while only paying with one dissonant material, on the other hand, makes them second only to the Solars, and not particularly far. Right now, nobody but Solars can start resonant with the Artifact 4 they bought in chargen, and then be assured that when they loot an Artifact 5 off a foe's corpse, they'll be resonant with it.<br /> <br /> I might suggest instead that they be neutral with most magical materials, and then resonant with &quot;panchaloha&quot;. In real life, that's a Sanskrit term for term for a five-metal alloy used for making jewelry and temple statues. In Exalted for this purpose, it would designate a specially-made alloy of the 5MMs (maybe with adamant replacing soulsteel?). This would hold the Nocturnals approximately even with Lunars and Abyssals in affinity for magical materials (resonant with artifacts bought at character creation, neutral with most of what you could acquire by looting foes). It would make them worldbuilding-wise a rival of the Sidereals and Getimians in trying to acquire starmetal for making artifacts. And it would reflect the story of inability-to-commit in that all five wouuld have to be present for Nocturnals to be resonant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T22:30:50-07:00","id":1319406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319389#post1319389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might suggest instead that they be neutral with most magical materials, and then resonant with &quot;panchaloha&quot;. In real life, that's a Sanskrit term for term for a five-metal alloy used for making jewelry and temple statues. In Exalted for this purpose, it would designate a specially-made alloy of the 5MMs (maybe with adamant replacing soulsteel?). This would hold the Nocturnals approximately even with Lunars and Abyssals in affinity for magical materials (resonant with artifacts bought at character creation, neutral with most of what you could acquire by looting foes). It would make them worldbuilding-wise a rival of the Sidereals and Getimians in trying to acquire starmetal for making artifacts. And it would reflect the story of inability-to-commit in that all five would have to be present for Nocturnals to be resonant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under those circumstances, we could then make them dissonant with soulsteel, as the lost potential of those souls (and their future reincarnations) clash with their natural predisposition for possibilities. Combined with the historic rarity of the metal, it wouldn't be too far off the mark.<br /> <br /> As for cutting down the keywords for charms, I can get behind that, though I would suggest the removed keywords aare noted under possible themes for Nocturnal charm types. I like Lunars, but until the 3e splatbook, they were a thematic mess with poor mechanical support. The TAW Fan project was arguably the best version of them because of how tight the charms concepts were to the themes.<br /> Bringing a simular mentality (say, 2-4 thematic statements per attribute) might be useful and the discarded keywords could easily serve as inspiration for that purpose.<br /> <br /> Can we find a way to get rid of the Curse of Subservience though? I fail to see a way any good can come of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T07:45:46-07:00","id":1319461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319370#post1319370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Storytelling chapter like there was in the 2E pdf could be very useful. It could discuss types of games you can run with Nocturnals Protagonists, present how to use them as Antagonists, suggest ways the ST can play out the bits of Lore that are left intentionally vague, and include information about the Manvantara and the 6th Caste in the event those things make the transition to 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Iceblade has said, the reason that there is no mention of a Storytelling chapter is that in 3e, the core splat books lack one. I guess they assume that the splat's book should have enough information to run them as antagonists and protagonists. Just to note that the 6th Caste is shown at the traits chapter, and Manvantara (or any other presentation for an alternative worlds) could be presented as its own chapter- even though I'm a bit wary of touching that subject before Getimians are out, as each of those is a lost worldline. I'm not saying we should ignore that part, but if we'll include it it should be its own chapter and after the nature of the Nocturnals will be decided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T07:56:21-07:00","id":1319463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319372#post1319372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Civilizations, I don't think Nocturnals should get stuff as iconic as Lunar Dominions but that doesn't mean they shouldn't get anything. Creation is a big big place, much of it still empty. adding more shit won't hurt it much, well as long as it fits with the others, and I think it would be fun to see what type of factions develop among the Night's Chosen. How much would they be independent, and how many have found themselves under another Exalts command. I also think that if you are gonna include the Firmament that would be a good place to put it, how and why its a realm, whether it interacts with the rest like Yu Shan, what you can expect there and Caelain City, which would probably make a nice center of Nocturnal activity, as much as Great Forks is to Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, more or less- even though I think the theme of the Nocturnals should be that things are not constant, and as such things like powerful civilizations and social constructs kinds works against their theme of temporary wonders and miracles. Having some centers of of culture to the Nocturnals, be them on the Firmament or Creation, as well as perhaps a few cultures which express the nature of the Nocturnals may be interesting. Something to think about when we'll find their place in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And lastly, talking about the Nocturnals Charm keywords, looking over on the pdf. One thing I can certainly say is that I think that got a bit to many so yeah they probably should be revised. Personally I think the one relating to Calibration is to specific to be practical, that and I think Nox shouldn't be made God of Calibration again. Mostly because I feel that should be Five Day's Darkness thing. I think that is fine as is. Or thats how I think anyway </div> </div> </div>I think that in 2e, Nox could have got away with becoming the Calibration King as he lost many, many things when he was weaved into the Loom of Fate. Currently, we even haven't decided if he is in the same state or not. I think we should focus on him more as the God of the Night, a title which was taken by Luna after whatever happened that happened (if happened. I assume that the Lunars would call Nox and his Chosen liars and usurpers if they'll claim that Luna stole Nox's mantle. Something to think about).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:04:33-07:00","id":1319466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319389#post1319389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the PC-creation level, making them neutral with everything effectively makes them worse than everybody else (except Liminals) with artifacts and Evocations. Sure, from a worldbuilding perspective they're better off than Sidereals and Getimians, since starmetal's rare and those two are dissonant with everything else. But when doing character creation, you just specify that the artifact you bought with your dots is of the material you're resonant with.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being able to choose a temporarily-resonant material while only paying with one dissonant material, on the other hand, makes them second only to the Solars, and not particularly far. Right now, nobody but Solars can start resonant with the Artifact 4 they bought in chargen, and then be assured that when they loot an Artifact 5 off a foe's corpse, they'll be resonant with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to note that the Umbrals are also going to be Neutral with all materials (not to deny anything that you said, but just a note). Keeping a game balance is something I would want help with, so thank you for the notes. Of course, we haven't decided about the exact mechanics for such &quot;resonance manipulation&quot;, but if there are simpler solutions which are still on theme than why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I might suggest instead that they be neutral with most magical materials, and then resonant with &quot;panchaloha&quot;. In real life, that's a Sanskrit term for term for a five-metal alloy used for making jewelry and temple statues. In Exalted for this purpose, it would designate a specially-made alloy of the 5MMs (maybe with adamant replacing soulsteel?). This would hold the Nocturnals approximately even with Lunars and Abyssals in affinity for magical materials (resonant with artifacts bought at character creation, neutral with most of what you could acquire by looting foes). It would make them worldbuilding-wise a rival of the Sidereals and Getimians in trying to acquire starmetal for making artifacts. And it would reflect the story of inability-to-commit in that all five wouuld have to be present for Nocturnals to be resonant. </div> </div> </div>That actually sounds really cool! I assume that it could be expanded into an whole &quot;alloy system&quot; which details the level of resonance according to the number and types of materials the artifact includes, with panchaloha being the &quot;most refined&quot;- but that may be too complicated, and perhaps we should maintain simplicity. A really nice concept for Nocturnals, I must say. Maybe we could play around with the two concepts, with Panchaloha being regular &quot;resonant&quot; object, and perhaps under certain conditions Nocturnals could gain resonance with Starmetal/Moonsilver/Adamant (with such conditions being built in a way which maintains balance). Just something to think about, of course. We are still at brainstorming state right now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:23:18-07:00","id":1319470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts#post1318724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we find a way to get rid of the Curse of Subservience though? I fail to see a way any good can come of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some players seem to really enjoy it though, because it's the basis for Harlequin theme of being servants who outwit their masters. Maybe there could be a way to make it optional. For instance, maybe Nocturnals took part in the Primordial war but fought on both sides, so those who helped the Primordials have the Curse of Subservience while those who helped the Exalted Host toil under the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319461#post1319461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Iceblade has said, the reason that there is no mention of a Storytelling chapter is that in 3e, the core splat books lack one. I guess they assume that the splat's book should have enough information to run them as antagonists and protagonists. Just to note that the 6th Caste is shown at the traits chapter, and Manvantara (or any other presentation for an alternative worlds) could be presented as its own chapter- even though I'm a bit wary of touching that subject before Getimians are out, as each of those is a lost worldline. I'm not saying we should ignore that part, but if we'll include it it should be its own chapter and after the nature of the Nocturnals will be decided.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, official splats will be able to make up for their lack of a Storytelling chapter with the official ST book which will cover every splat, even those not yet released. By contrast, fanmade splats like Nocturnals have to be complete out of the gate since they won't get a separate book to discuss their Storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:29:00-07:00","id":1319471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319406#post1319406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for cutting down the keywords for charms, I can get behind that, though I would suggest the removed keywords aare noted under possible themes for Nocturnal charm types. I like Lunars, but until the 3e splatbook, they were a thematic mess with poor mechanical support. The TAW Fan project was arguably the best version of them because of how tight the charms concepts were to the themes.<br /> Bringing a simular mentality (say, 2-4 thematic statements per attribute) might be useful and the discarded keywords could easily serve as inspiration for that purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I am too in favor of minimizing keywords. Maintaining a few, solid themes is much better than diluting the concept with too many of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can we find a way to get rid of the Curse of Subservience though? I fail to see a way any good can come of it. </div> </div> </div>I mean, we could remove the Curse of Subservience form Nocturnals- but then they won't really be Nocturnals anymore.<br /> <br /> I mean, most of the Nocturnals' presentation is based around their themes as Heralds and Harlequins- mostly the later. Their history, concepts and attitude toward the world is centered around their Curse and its influence upon them, making them into servants, arlecchinos, harlequins. They are tricksters and jesters, but not like the Joker or Loki, but like the djinn, monkey paws and other wish granters- they would grant your wishes, but be careful what you wish for. It also worked with Nox's nature as a bound god, and them being chosen from those bound by fate.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying we keep things as the same- Nox may still be bound, he may be not. We have already considered them showing up during the First Age instead of the Time of Tumult. Adamant resonance was removed both because the original writer said they were not satisfied with the concept and, mostly, because the Hearteaters have that niche. Nox's role as the &quot;forbidden Incarna&quot; is being considered due to the Umbrals having a patron described similarly (even though it may be one of the optional origin stories). And of course, we need to deal with the Getimians, for which we try to work to tone down some of the tension between Nocturnals and Sidereals to make sure they work as companion splats, instead of foils. But the Curse is iconic- it is the reason for their title, and a significant factor for the Nocturnal experience, putting the ultimate conflict of &quot;freedom vs servitude&quot; in the very heart of the splat.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I personally like the Curse- I'm not saying we should keep it as is, far from it. It should be revised and changed especially as it causes a bad tension between the Nocturnals and the Celestials, not to mention it reinforce that Dragon Blooded are not &quot;true Exalts&quot; (and of course, with new Exalts in the game, how can you define Celestial and Terrestrial anymore?). My suggestion for tying it into their intimacies (and I'm not saying &quot;if you have an intimacy you must serve the person it leans toward to&quot;, only that the mechanics would revolve around the Nocturnal being compelled to follow those they feel attached to) makes it that the true person the Nocturnals are bound to is themselves- you are a slave to your own passions, something which they share with their patron and his attempts to side with and satisfy everyone.<br /> <br /> Now, I know that some people don't like giving so much agency over their character to another character- we can even see proofs for that discussion in the pdf, were a standard &quot;Great Curse&quot; was presented as an alternative. But the thing is that I really, truly, love Nocturnals- with all of their themes as servants, fate twisters and wish makers, miracles of the night and chosen of possibilities. I don't want to &quot;fix&quot; them, because I don't think they need to be fixed- only to be revised and adapted to fit 3e's setting and themes (which is easier said than done). As it is a fan project, anyone who doesn't like the Curse could easily make their own variants of it once the splat will be written- but I'm going to keep its concept in this project, and do my best to adapt it in the most satisfying way and make sure to both stay true to the Nocturnals origin and story and make it as compelling to fun to play as I possibly can.<br /> <br /> So in short- I think we should at least try to adapt the original themes of the Curse to 3e before getting rid of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT- I hope this don't come of as offensive. I usually try to not be passionate about things online, but I have a really warm place in my heart for the Nocturnals. I don't try top say that you don't love the Nocturnals, or that there is only one right way to play them, but I do wish that before people would just rule out some aspect of Nocturnals, that first we'll try to adapt and revise it so it could be judged properly. If that won't work, well, we do have Epitome's compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-19-2019, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:31:48-07:00","id":1319473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319463#post1319463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in 2e, Nox could have got away with becoming the Calibration King as he lost many, many things when he was weaved into the Loom of Fate. Currently, we even haven't decided if he is in the same state or not. I think we should focus on him more as the God of the Night, a title which was taken by Luna after whatever happened that happened (if happened. I assume that the Lunars would call Nox and his Chosen liars and usurpers if they'll claim that Luna stole Nox's mantle. Something to think about).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, Luna isnt the only Night God in 3e. The Uncounquered Sun is as well. Specifically he's called the God of Day and Night, thus denoting his role as a signifier of time. While Luna was the called the Priemier Goddess of Night among other domains as well. So both gods kinda budge into it but with different themes, same how Nox's Night is different and just ain't plain darkness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:34:59-07:00","id":1319474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319470#post1319470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, official splats will be able to make up for their lack of a Storytelling chapter with the official ST book which will cover every splat, even those not yet released. By contrast, fanmade splats like Nocturnals have to be complete out of the gate since they won't get a separate book to discuss their Storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a point there- but let's deal with it when the time would come. It is an important aspect, sure- but I think it is kind of low priority next to other things in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:42:41-07:00","id":1319476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319466#post1319466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just wanted to note that the Umbrals are also going to be Neutral with all materials (not to deny anything that you said, but just a note). Keeping a game balance is something I would want help with, so thank you for the notes. Of course, we haven't decided about the exact mechanics for such &quot;resonance manipulation&quot;, but if there are simpler solutions which are still on theme than why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> That actually sounds really cool! I assume that it could be expanded into an whole &quot;alloy system&quot; which details the level of resonance according to the number and types of materials the artifact includes, with panchaloha being the &quot;most refined&quot;- but that may be too complicated, and perhaps we should maintain simplicity. A really nice concept for Nocturnals, I must say. Maybe we could play around with the two concepts, with Panchaloha being regular &quot;resonant&quot; object, and perhaps under certain conditions Nocturnals could gain resonance with Starmetal/Moonsilver/Adamant (with such conditions being built in a way which maintains balance). Just something to think about, of course. We are still at brainstorming state right now</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea is probably just keep them as flat neutral to most materials,(Except Soulsteel, While Jade isn't really Celestial you can fit it in with how the Aurora Caste work) and then have this Panchaloha(probably needs a neater name, or a few.) as a result of a Crafting Charm that Nocturnals have. Since if this would answer if this alloy was a thing, why aren't the other Chosen aware of it, and have as a certain little trick Nocturnals developed to attune with their Essences. Something like that. That way you can frankly give them just Neutrals but have a work around to make it not so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T08:44:24-07:00","id":1319479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319474#post1319474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a point there- but let's deal with it when the time would come. It is an important aspect, sure- but I think it is kind of low priority next to other things in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree, a ST chapter would have to be done last anyway since it depends on literally everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T06:49:49-07:00","id":1319916,"title":"","content":"So let's start from the history section, shall we?<br /> <br /> What I've had in mind for the Nocturnals is to have around 5-6 different origin stories, all dating back to the early First Age, either during or shortly after the Divine Revolution. That is a big difference compared to the other Exalts, as we know exactly from where did they came from and why- but I think that as the god of the night, sky and possibilities, it makes sense for Nox to try and not define his or his Chosen's nature. Perhaps none of the stories are true, perhaps all of them are- it is Nox's nature to provide contradicting options and fulfill them all in the same time. Each of the stories may reflect a different side of Nox, for the Midnight King could never be defined through a single story.<br /> <br /> The main reason, IMO, to move the entrance of the Nocturnals from the Time of Tumult to the First Age is due to the fact that there are already enough Exalts which show up in modern times- the return of the Solars, the awakening of Exigence, the inversion of the Abyssals, the creation of Infernals, the release of the Getimians, the corruption of Gloam's Dragon Blooded.. heck, even the invasion of the Alchemicals may count. There are enough Exalts plaguing Creation as modern dangers, the Nocturnals may serve better as coming into public existence much earlier.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the origin of the Nocrtunals is only a part of the story- for we need to think what the Nocturnals have actually done through the whole time they existed. What were their relations with the other Exalted Host during the First Age? Did they participated in the Niobraran War? Who did they supported in the Usurpation? Heck, which side they even took in the Divine Revolution, if any? Are the Nocturnals going to constantly choose the two sides in every conflict? Because if so, it would have been only a matter of time before the Solars would grow mad and unleash their wrath upon Night's Chosen. Perhaps during the Niobraran, the Solars were the ones to kill and banish the Nocturnals from the world, seemingly with the help of the Sidereals- even though that perhaps the Sidereals actually planned their eventual survival in one way or another?<br /> <br /> Would the Nocturnals, then, return after the Usuraption? Or perhaps after the Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusades, when the &quot;Gates of Night&quot; in which their Exaltations were held prisoners were broken, giving Creation a new possibility to rise above its ruined state. What have they done in those times? As we mentioned earlier, they are unlikely to have produced realms and nations around themselves- well, perhaps not all of them. Maybe they were trapped, in fact, in the mysterious Firmament, were they have started a strange culture which revolves around the strange land? Where they hunted by the Realm as Anathema? Have they sided with the Dragon Blooded, or worked against the Bronze Faction?<br /> <br /> What have they done in the years of the Realm's rule? How do they react to the events after the Empress has vanished? Are they worried of the return of the Solars, or do they see in it as a chance for a change? Are there Nocturnal Elders still around, few beings which have either roamed Creation or watch from the Firmament for centuries, while living under countless false identities and persona? <br /> <br /> And most important than all- what is Nox? Is he indeed a lost brother to the Maidens, as he claim he is? Or perhaps he is just an impostor, liar and a thief who took power and title which were not his own? Does Nox even exist, or perhaps he is a future yet to come.. or a past long erased? What kind of game does Nox play, if he plays a game at all? Is he still weaved into the Loom of Fate, from which he whispers strange possibilities to the path of fate? or is he an Indigo Jester, which brings change wherever he goes for the sake of chaos alone?<br /> <br /> And other thoughts like that :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T08:30:46-07:00","id":1319933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1319916#post1319916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's start from the history section, shall we?<br /> <br /> What I've had in mind for the Nocturnals is to have around 5-6 different origin stories, all dating back to the early First Age, either during or shortly after the Divine Revolution. That is a big difference compared to the other Exalts, as we know exactly from where did they came from and why- but I think that as the god of the night, sky and possibilities, it makes sense for Nox to try and not define his or his Chosen's nature. Perhaps none of the stories are true, perhaps all of them are- it is Nox's nature to provide contradicting options and fulfill them all in the same time. Each of the stories may reflect a different side of Nox, for the Midnight King could never be defined through a single story.<br /> <br /> The main reason, IMO, to move the entrance of the Nocturnals from the Time of Tumult to the First Age is due to the fact that there are already enough Exalts which show up in modern times- the return of the Solars, the awakening of Exigence, the inversion of the Abyssals, the creation of Infernals, the release of the Getimians, the corruption of Gloam's Dragon Blooded.. heck, even the invasion of the Alchemicals may count. There are enough Exalts plaguing Creation as modern dangers, the Nocturnals may serve better as coming into public existence much earlier.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the origin of the Nocrtunals is only a part of the story- for we need to think what the Nocturnals have actually done through the whole time they existed. What were their relations with the other Exalted Host during the First Age? Did they participated in the Niobraran War? Who did they supported in the Usurpation? Heck, which side they even took in the Divine Revolution, if any? Are the Nocturnals going to constantly choose the two sides in every conflict? Because if so, it would have been only a matter of time before the Solars would grow mad and unleash their wrath upon Night's Chosen. Perhaps during the Niobraran, the Solars were the ones to kill and banish the Nocturnals from the world, seemingly with the help of the Sidereals- even though that perhaps the Sidereals actually planned their eventual survival in one way or another?<br /> <br /> Would the Nocturnals, then, return after the Usuraption? Or perhaps after the Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusades, when the &quot;Gates of Night&quot; in which their Exaltations were held prisoners were broken, giving Creation a new possibility to rise above its ruined state. What have they done in those times? As we mentioned earlier, they are unlikely to have produced realms and nations around themselves- well, perhaps not all of them. Maybe they were trapped, in fact, in the mysterious Firmament, were they have started a strange culture which revolves around the strange land? Where they hunted by the Realm as Anathema? Have they sided with the Dragon Blooded, or worked against the Bronze Faction?<br /> <br /> What have they done in the years of the Realm's rule? How do they react to the events after the Empress has vanished? Are they worried of the return of the Solars, or do they see in it as a chance for a change? Are there Nocturnal Elders still around, few beings which have either roamed Creation or watch from the Firmament for centuries, while living under countless false identities and persona?<br /> <br /> And most important than all- what is Nox? Is he indeed a lost brother to the Maidens, as he claim he is? Or perhaps he is just an impostor, liar and a thief who took power and title which were not his own? Does Nox even exist, or perhaps he is a future yet to come.. or a past long erased? What kind of game does Nox play, if he plays a game at all? Is he still weaved into the Loom of Fate, from which he whispers strange possibilities to the path of fate? or is he an Indigo Jester, which brings change wherever he goes for the sake of chaos alone?<br /> <br /> And other thoughts like that :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple Choice Origins does sound good. Though 5/6 may be to much to come up with. Something like 3/4 might be easier to make them all consistent with each other.<br /> <br /> I agree that I like the idea of them showing up in the First Age, though I haven't decided yet whether they should have showed up in the War of the Gods or not and thats how the devision of Harlequins and Heralds came about. I would think that with their Curse, the Nocturnals would be on the side of whoever they had their loyalties. Which would be both typically. Even the Niobaran War had not only the Spoken on the side of the Sea, but Solars, Lunars, and Dragon-Blooded who came from their. Being Exalted from fish and aquatic folk.<br /> <br /> One idea I have though, instead of the Nocturnals being trapped by the others, they were the ones that purposefully left Creation. They who would be able to see and experience the madness of the Solars and see the coming tensions, instead of getting themselves involved with either side of the conflict by opposing lieges, They would instead all opt to get the hell out of dodge and through some powerful sorcery by leading sorcerers in its Host, would escape to the Firmament which they either discovered, repurposed, or created entirely. Thus having a safe haven, as much as they could. It was only later did they decided to go back into the world, spurned on by advocates who didn't want to abandoned Creation to its disasters. I could see the Firmament being seen as a sort of sanctuary for the Nocturnals, A place they have when they need to hide or to not feel the burden of their Curse.<br /> <br /> I would think that with the Nocturnals hidden nature it would be hard for them to be classified as whole as Anathema. As for alleginences. That could possibly go all ways. Whether its Bronze, or Gold. The Silver Pact or the Realm.<br /> <br /> As for Nox, I would think that his origin would be wrapped up in much theories and mysteries by his Chosen. I would go with that all modern Harlequins wouldn't be any survivors from the Primordial War, that even if they did pop up around the First Age they were already under the Curse. Even in the escape to the Firmament, all their scholars could do is speculate from their Essence, vague dreams, and from pieces into Fate. They are probably aware of some certain facts about Nox, that he is Incarna, God of Possibilities and the Night Sky. That he has a relationship with the Five Maidens, speculating that he's a lost brother. They can possibly speculate that he's in the Loom. That would one way explain their mystifying nature but they probably don't have much to prove it on. This could also maybe play up with the Heralds, that they might be the only ones who know of the truth, whether they are survivors of the Divine Rebellion or capable of hearing Nox's clear voice and messages, without obscurity. That's an idea anyhow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-21-2019, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T11:37:38-07:00","id":1320123,"title":"","content":"So here are some concepts I have for the origin section of the Nocturnals- I just wish to stress that unlike certain mysteries in the setting, those are not going to be &quot;the truth is unknown in the setting, here are some options for you to choose the truth&quot;, but &quot;the truth is unknown in the setting, here are some popular theories the Nocturnals themselves tell&quot;. Also, in the spirit of 3e, I've decided to try and focus those origins around the Chosen themselves, as 3e seems to put the Exalted on the backstage and the gods in the background. I would also like to emphasis that each of those origins should be no more than a paragraph or two- the Primordial War is a much more distant event, and it isn't much discussed in the books as such.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's what I got-<br /> <br /> 1) Nox the Betrayer- Nox was an Incrana, the God of Night's Sky. While his siblings shared with him the secrets of Exaltations, he was secretly planning to sell them to the enemies of the gods and use his Chosen as soldiers against the armies of the gods. However, as his Chosen walked the earth, they learned of the harsh rule of the ancients and the terrors they brought upon Creation. Seeing the error in their patron's ways, the armies of the Nocturnals were split into two- one side following the will of Nox, and the other rebelling against it. The war was dreadful, but in the end, those who were on the side of the gods were victorious, and Nox was captured. While the punishment for such treachery would have been death, those Nocturnals which supported the armies of heaven pledged for mercy for both their siblings and patron, and as such Nox's life were spared- but his mind and body were broken, and weaved into the the Firmament beyond the Gates of Night, were it would suffer in eternal exile.<br /> <br /> 2) Nox the Betrayed- Nox was an Incrana, the God of Night's Sky. Following the plot of his siblings, he too made Chosen of his own to supplement the armies of the gods. Yet Nox was a lonesome god, never a true part of the Incrana and too close to the ancients. Fearing a change of heart and with the prophecies of the Maidens giving contradictory results, they decide to act in advance. As such, on the eve of the Divine Revolution, Nox was lost, tempted, defeated, hidden and ended, while his Chosen were sent to the war under his name. Yet the Nocturnals were suspicious, and while they sided with the armies of heaven at first, they have wondered why their god didn't came to support them in the war. Secretly, Night's Chosen have searched a possibility beyond that decided by fate, and managed to discovered their broken deity beyond the Gates of Night. Furious, many of the Nocturnals have withdrew their support and turned to serve the enemies, while others, bound by their loyalty to the fellow Exalts, staid on the side of the gods- a choice which was, apparently, the correct one.<br /> <br /> 3) Nox the Loyal- Nox was an Incrana, the God of Night's Sky. Seeing the endless possibilities which the future had to offer, he was never much of a decisive individual- and when he learned of the plans of his siblings, his heart was torn. He loved his siblings, especially the Maidens which he saw as actual sisters, and as such wanted the best for them. However, he also loved the ancients, which he saw as his parents, as they were the ones who made everything possible. Looking at the endless possibilities, Nox has decided to support both sides as best he could, knowing that it would cost him dearly. He supported both sides before the war, helping them as much as he could to build their forces with revealing the plot. When he granted the miracle of Exaltation to his Chosen, he divided them into two- one half, he guided to support the gods. The other half, he sent to serve the ancients. On the eve of the war, he waited for the very last moment before his heart broke, and he ran to warn the ancients in advance- yet his sisters knew what was in his heart, and they knew they had too much too lose if the warning would come on time. With heavy heart, the Maidens defeated Nox and imprisoned him beyond the Gates of Night, while his Chosen went to war against each other, their heart torn like that of their patron.<br /> <br /> 4) Nox the Mastermind- Nox was an Incarna, the God of Night's Sky. Seen as inferior by the ancients, Nox has always resented and envied their rule upon the world, as they bound him to their service. Seen as inferior by the Sun and Luna, Nox has always resented and envied the light they cast upon the world, as they force him as their servant. Among the other Incarna, only the Maidens were somewhat close to him, and even they were never trusted by the lonely god. Hearing the plans of the coming Divine Rebellion, Nox has gleefully agreed to support the gods in their plot- yet with his heart filled with resentment and envy, he made plans of his own, hoping to turn his enemies against one another and become the new king of both Day and Night. As he made his Chosen, he secretly divided them into two armies- one to support the gods, and one to support the ancients. On the night of the Divine Revolution, Nox has quickly went to warn the ancients, as he knew that it would turn the war even bloodier- but the Maidens knew their brother's dark heart, and turned his passions against him. As his Chosen clashed against one another in the battlefield, Nox's mind and body were broken, and he was thrown beyond the Gates of Night- yet, dreadfully, he was laughing through the whole process, for his plan worked. There, on the desolated planes of the Firmament, neither the ancients nor the Incrana were to rule over him. There, finally, he was free. There, finally, his true plan could begin.<br /> <br /> 5) Nox the Jester- Nox was an Incarna, the God of Night's Sky. Unlike the rest of his siblings, Nox never had higher inspirations in his life. Serving as a jester in the courts of the ancients, his only goal was chaos, pure and simple. When the other Incrana informed him of their plans to rebel against the ancients, Nox agreed, believing that the war would change the status que and produce many possibilities in the future to explore. Wishing the war to be as chaotic as possible, he has secretly divided his Chosen with secret commands- one part to serve the gods as the heralds of the future to come, and one part to serve the ancients as harlequins of change and possibility. As the war grew closer, Nox noticed that the possibilities for winning tilted more and more toward the side of the gods, making him bored with the plans for the future- until a spark of inspiration burned in his mind. In the night before the war, Nox has cloaked his figure and secretly went to warn the ancients of the coming rebellion, believing it would even the odds and make the result less predictable- yet the Incrana knew their sibling's nature, and took precautions. The Maiden foresaw his steps, tracked him down and subdued him. While his Chosen fought one another, the Sun judged Nox to be broken and exiled beyond the Gates of Night- and as he heard the verdict, Nox was thrilled and laughed, for of all the possibilities the future held, that was the only one he never considered.<br /> <br /> 6) Nox the False- Nox was not an Incarna, and definitely not the God of Night's Sky. Nox came from beyond the Gates of Night, a strange entity of unknown origin, a failed divinity banished long, long ago. For ages, Nox was trapped in the Firmament which he called home, able to only watch Creation, but never to act. However, as the war against the ancients raged, the enemies of the gods grew desperate. They broke the seal upon the Gates of Night, and summoned the Midnight King to supply them in the war. As he watched carefully through the rise of the Exalts and the course of the war, Nox knew a lot about the process of Exaltation, and as such was able to produce Chosen of his own- even though the act has diminished him, breaking his mind and body while his Essence got tangled to that of his home. However, as Nox has granted soldiers to the armies of the ancients, he has done the same to the armies of the gods- which has suddenly discovered new Exalts of unknown origin walking among them, rising their spears next to them and fighting the ancients together with them. To both sides, Nox has started to whisper lies and falsehoods- that he was a kin to the Incarna, a grand God of the Night, either fighting alongside them or against them. And when the war has ended and the gods claimed victory, they discovered the broken Gates of Night which they quickly sealed- yet it was too late. Nox may have been bound to his throne- but the Nocturnals were free, and with them, the possibility for a different future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-22-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T12:06:19-07:00","id":1320130,"title":"","content":"Hm, what is the difference between the Gates of Night and the Firmament, is the Gates what Night appears to mortals and the Firmaments beyond that or what?. Also is you idea of the Firmament where Nox is bound and woven then, instead of the Loom? If so neat. Though this does remind I wonder what's gonna be the exact relationship with the Stars and Loom 3e. Well that's one more thing to look forward for Sidereals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T12:26:17-07:00","id":1320132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320130#post1320130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, what is the difference between the Gates of Night and the Firmament, is the Gates what Night appears to mortals and the Firmaments beyond that or what?. Also is you idea of the Firmament where Nox is bound and woven then, instead of the Loom? If so neat. Though this does remind I wonder what's gonna be the exact relationship with the Stars and Loom 3e. Well that's one more thing to look forward for Sidereals</div> </div> </div> </div>In this concept, the Gates of Night are the boundary between Creation and the Firmament. Still not sure about their nature, or even if they are a physical place or a phenomenon/ metaphor (like, when someone goes to the Firmament you say that they have &quot;passed through the Gates of Night&quot;). And yes, the idea is the Nox's Essence is now a part of the Firmament. I've thought it would enhance the importance of the realm, and would make it more creepy (as it is the only place where you can feel and commune with Nox directly- which is not necessarily a nice experience :P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T08:57:04-07:00","id":1320288,"title":"","content":"Hm, here's a brainstorm my own. My proposal and take for the Nocturnals history written up the style of splats intros, albeit roughly. Critiques and thoughts are welcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History of the Nocturnal Exalted</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Time Before, long before the Incarnae raised up their champions for war. It has been said that there once existed a God, now lost. His name was Nox, God of Possibilities, Incarna of the Night Sky. Who was the God of Night, none can say. They say he was many things, brother of the Five Maidens, emissary of the world\u2019s makers, traitor to the Incanae, a mad broken god, all and none of the above. Nox is defined by mystery, by contradiction, by paradox. He is a god long gone, broken and bound. Only remembered by the mark he left on Creation. Of his Chosen<br /> <br /> Like their patron, the origins of the nature of the Nocturnal Exalted is also a mystery, while they were uplifted from the ranks of mortals like the other champions of the gods, whether they rose to support the Gods or rose to tear them down, the answer has been lost to time. What can be certain is the during the War of the Gods the Nocturnal Host was split, fighting on both sides on conflict and that on the defeated was laid down a mighty curse to help bound the fluctuating nature of the Night's Chosen, to help support the Exalted Host rather then be against it.<br /> <br /> In the time of the First Age, the Harlequins drifted through the courts of the Exalted. Bound by pact, they never took power for themselves, but rather went on to serve the interests of others. They danced, fought, and entertained for the masses of Creation and its Exalted lords as marvelous and mysterious courtesans, gladiators, and jesters. They reveled in both in the whispers of the rumored and the glories of the spectacular, living as walking, breathing, laughing contradictions. The Chosen of the Night weren\u2019t slaves however, bound as they might be. For they are as much capable in bringing revolution and coup d'etat against the wicked as they are in bringing about wonders and revelations to the joyful. Where the Nocturnals came, change quickly followed in their steps.<br /> <br /> On the eve of the Usurpation, from observations on the behaviors of their masters and patrons, as well as benefiting from some leaked correspondences from the Sidereal Exalted, who often served as partners, minders, and companions to the Nocturnals, the Nocturnal Exalted were far to aware of the coming tension between the Exalted Host. Seeing themselves trapped by chains of loyalty and oath that threatened to bring themselves against each other once again, in their desperation the Nocturnal Host opted to abandon the coming conflict and all their obligations with it. Through mighty magic and sorcery, the Nocturnals broke open the Gates of Night and in mass escaped to the broken form of the God of Night Sky. Thus they disappeared from the face of the world, leaving only legends and folktales.<br /> <br /> In coming centuries, few Nocturnals left the bounds of the Firmament. Once again becoming embroiled in the schemes and intrigues of the Exalted, of the wars of the Shogunate and Silver Pack. Others choose to ignore the kingdoms and realms of the other Chosen, instead wandering among mortals across the Threshold, becoming heroes and tyrants without abandoned as they tied their interests to the plights and loves of those that caught their eye. As a whole though, the Nocturnal Host secluded themselves among the broken stars of the Firmament, living in revelry and celebration in the Caelian City, the heart of the Firmament and a city that ever changes. In those days, they kept to themselves willfully abandoning Creation as they distracted themselves with pleasures and dreams unimagined, bound to no one.<br /> <br /> Now in the Times of Tumult, things are starting to change. Mysterious self-proclaimed Heralds have rose from among Nocturnals, their motives obscure and origins a mystery. They say they speak in enigmas, claiming to hear the voice of Nox, their natures frequently shifting. They speak out amongst the Night's Chosen, saying that the time has come to return to Creation, that the future is in flux and a new era comes. New possibilities have appeared they say, new chances, and its time for the Nocturnals to claim it. To make themselves a new future. The Heralds speak, and many listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T11:06:17-07:00","id":1320315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320288#post1320288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, here's a brainstorm my own. My proposal and take for the Nocturnals history written up the style of splats intros, albeit roughly. Critiques and thoughts are welcome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, some thoughts about the section-<br /> <br /> First, I do like the obscure approach to the Nocturnal history. It is well consistent with the other books, and it does fit 3e's writing style, so well done for that.<br /> <br /> As for the Curse- I would just want to note that while I do like the idea of it, as I've mentioned before, I think it would benefit much from not tying the servitude of the Nocturnals to Exalted only. The idea of the curse would be to insure loyalty, and the Solars would have utilized it by making themselves so much important in the life of the Nocturnals so that they would be compelled to obey them. I do like the way you portray the 1st age Harlequins and their function in the Old Realm.<br /> <br /> Some issue with the isolation of the Nocturnals- while it does gives an explanation for where the Nocturnals have been through all of this time, the outcome is that the vast majority of Nocturnals have done practically nothing in the time they spent on the Firmament. Spending all of their existence with celebrations is kinda boring after a few generations- the Nocturnals should be more active, either establishing their presence upon an alien world where their god is bound and whispering, or taking an active part in the life of Creation. Also, there is an issue that they have no reason to return to Creation, other than the Heralds telling them to. I suggest to both develop what the Nocturnals actually did in the Firmament, and to strength the ties between Creation and the Firmament- that would help to different them from the Alchemicals, which also live on a separate world until they suddenly return to Creation. Creation is a wide world, returning Nocturnals could do a lot of things in it without being noticed for something other than Exigents. Not to mention that as Harlequins, it kinda goes against their theme to stay outside of Creation without any &quot;master to serve&quot;. I do like the distinction between a &quot;servant&quot; and a &quot;slave&quot; and the writeup, which is an important one.<br /> <br /> The writeup also lacks a very important point- connection to the Sidereal Exalted. The Nocturnals are the companion splat to the Sidereals, after all- they should be dominant in their history as much as the Solars are dominant in the Lunars. While we are still working on the exact relationships the two splats would have, removing the Sidereal- Nocturnal connection would harm the identity of the Nocturnals, IMO.<br /> <br /> Finally, we should establish what the Heralds are and where they come from. I think that a nice twist would be that instead of making the Heralds those Nocturnals which have sided with the gods in the Divine Revolution, they would be those which have sided with the Primordials. After the war was ended, the Exalted Hosts have decided that they could not trust those strange Exalts- those who turned against them were executed and locked back in the Firmament, while those who supported them were bound to serve, so to make sure they will not betray them (something which didn't quit worked, as Nox's nature twisted the curse from being bound to their Exalted, to be bound to their passions). Perhaps with the opening of the Gates of Night, the Heralds were freed and connected back to Creation, and so while the Harlequins were establishing their presence upon the Firmament the Heralds have traveled Creation, hiding their existence from their siblings while working on plans of their own.<br /> <br /> So in short, the main criticisms I have are that the Nocturnals need to do more (remember that one of the criticisms about the Lunars in 1e was that they just sat in the Wyld and were doing nothing, IIRC), they need a good connection to the Sidereals and they need a clarification about who are the Heralds and where they have been through all of this time. The writeup should also clarify the nature of the Curse, and how it has effected the life of the Nocturnals in the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T11:27:38-07:00","id":1320320,"title":"","content":"Also- I have just thought about a cool suggestion. If the Harlequins are the ones which supported the gods in the Divine Revolution, what if the &quot;Curse of Subservience&quot; is not, in fact, a curse? What if after the war, in order to show their loyalty to the Exalted Host, without being demanded or forced to, the Nocturnals have pledged loyalty and bound themselves of their free will, to serve and gather the celestial light of their siblings by their passion and conviction? The Nocturnals chose to be Harlequins, and by doing so bound their Essence to masters they chose for themselves? I think it would portray them at a much more heroic light than them just being &quot;cursed by the Solars/Sidereals/gods/etc&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T12:31:32-07:00","id":1320333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320315#post1320315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, some thoughts about the section-<br /> <br /> First, I do like the obscure approach to the Nocturnal history. It is well consistent with the other books, and it does fit 3e's writing style, so well done for that.<br /> <br /> As for the Curse- I would just want to note that while I do like the idea of it, as I've mentioned before, I think it would benefit much from not tying the servitude of the Nocturnals to Exalted only. The idea of the curse would be to insure loyalty, and the Solars would have utilized it by making themselves so much important in the life of the Nocturnals so that they would be compelled to obey them. I do like the way you portray the 1st age Harlequins and their function in the Old Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>that they are, though I do admit I didn't make it clear. From what I meant, was that Nocturnals both served the interests of both the Exalted and mortals. The talk about them going about the masses in the third paragraph was to that. And the talk about the Threshold about them doing shit for those that catch their interest would also be part of that. The curse was more about fixing the Nocturnal behavior. Making it more consistent in how they did things, <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some issue with the isolation of the Nocturnals- while it does gives an explanation for where the Nocturnals have been through all of this time, the outcome is that the vast majority of Nocturnals have done practically nothing in the time they spent on the Firmament. Spending all of their existence with celebrations is kinda boring after a few generations- the Nocturnals should be more active, either establishing their presence upon an alien world where their god is bound and whispering, or taking an active part in the life of Creation. Also, there is an issue that they have no reason to return to Creation, other than the Heralds telling them to. I suggest to both develop what the Nocturnals actually did in the Firmament, and to strength the ties between Creation and the Firmament- that would help to different them from the Alchemicals, which also live on a separate world until they suddenly return to Creation. Creation is a wide world, returning Nocturnals could do a lot of things in it without being noticed for something other than Exigents. Not to mention that as Harlequins, it kinda goes against their theme to stay outside of Creation without any &quot;master to serve&quot;. I do like the distinction between a &quot;servant&quot; and a &quot;slave&quot; and the writeup, which is an important one. </div> </div> </div>yeah that makes sense, I'm on the idea that it was the Nocturnals that made the Caelian City this go. Mainly the themes of celebration was mostly to fit with how Caelian City was described in the previous home-brew. I'm not against with them doing more, I was mostly just expanding on what we had previously. Personally I would like to see Creation out activities to be mostly in the realm of individuals, keeping a majority of them in the Firmament. Though that doesn't paticularly say how many individuals that it is, I probably change few to some to be more vague, as you said Creation is a big place. Though of course I have no idea on how Noc factions would be like so thats very open to change. As for activities, its probably better to say that Nocturnals haven't done anything, I just wanted to convey that they haven't done anything that big that would change the situation of Creation that much. Thats how I see it yeah, though the Firmament isn't Creation after all<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The writeup also lacks a very important point- connection to the Sidereal Exalted. The Nocturnals are the companion splat to the Sidereals, after all- they should be dominant in their history as much as the Solars are dominant in the Lunars. While we are still working on the exact relationships the two splats would have, removing the Sidereal- Nocturnal connection would harm the identity of the Nocturnals, IMO. </div> </div> </div>yeah I also felt that, while I referenced them a bit I couldn't really get a feel on where to put it in, since I decided to only briefly to talk about Nox. Then again its as you said I'm don't really have good idea on how their relationship is now. So that's probably why couldn't get to fit. Once thats established, an extra paragraph on that would probably do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, we should establish what the Heralds are and where they come from. I think that a nice twist would be that instead of making the Heralds those Nocturnals which have sided with the gods in the Divine Revolution, they would be those which have sided with the Primordials. After the war was ended, the Exalted Hosts have decided that they could not trust those strange Exalts- those who turned against them were executed and locked back in the Firmament, while those who supported them were bound to serve, so to make sure they will not betray them (something which didn't quit worked, as Nox's nature twisted the curse from being bound to their Exalted, to be bound to their passions). Perhaps with the opening of the Gates of Night, the Heralds were freed and connected back to Creation, and so while the Harlequins were establishing their presence upon the Firmament the Heralds have traveled Creation, hiding their existence from their siblings while working on plans of their own.<br /> <br /> So in short, the main criticisms I have are that the Nocturnals need to do more (remember that one of the criticisms about the Lunars in 1e was that they just sat in the Wyld and were doing nothing, IIRC), they need a good connection to the Sidereals and they need a clarification about who are the Heralds and where they have been through all of this time. The writeup should also clarify the nature of the Curse, and how it has effected the life of the Nocturnals in the First Age. </div> </div> </div>Yeah my take on the Heralds, were just my thoughts on them, mainly to make them seem prominent and for them to fulfill their names as heralds, being the people who start getting the Nocturnals involved in the Times of Tumult. As for your take, my only slight would be the Exalted intentionally placing a curse on their allies to make them obey. Not to my tastes, but that about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-23-2019, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T13:13:47-07:00","id":1320340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320333#post1320333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> yeah that makes sense, I'm on the idea that it was the Nocturnals that made the Caelian City this go. Mainly the themes of celebration was mostly to fit with how Caelian City was described in the previous home-brew. I'm not against with them doing more, I was mostly just expanding on what we had previously. Personally I would like to see Creation out activities to be mostly in the realm of individuals, keeping a majority of them in the Firmament. Though that doesn't paticularly say how many individuals that it is, I probably change few to some to be more vague, as you said Creation is a big place. Though of course I have no idea on how Noc factions would be like so thats very open to change. As for activities, its probably better to say that Nocturnals haven't done anything, I just wanted to convey that they haven't done anything that big that would change the situation of Creation that much. Thats how I see it yeah, though the Firmament isn't Creation after all</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that Creation is a big place. The Nocturnals could do big things and it won't change the setting- as long as the main events of the setting (Usurpation, Great Contagion, rise of the Realm, etc) remain consistent, whole empires could rise and fall and it won't effect the course of history. We could even make a faction of Nocturnals having a war against the Realm and losing, or them being hunted by the Wyld Hunt, or even them establishing a few regional powers which are outside of the reach of the Realm, and the setting would stay consistent. As long as we don't do something too ridiculus, I think we could allow the Nocturnals a bit more reach in both the Firmament and Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yeah I also felt that, while I referenced them a bit I couldn't really get a feel on where to put it in, since I decided to only briefly to talk about Nox. Then again its as you said I'm don't really have good idea on how their relationship is now. So that's probably why couldn't get to fit. Once thats established, an extra paragraph on that would probably do it. </div> </div> </div>As the wordcount for the history section is about a page and a half from what I can see from both the Dragon Blooded and the Lunars books, we have more than enough time to develop a number of important events which signify the special connection the Sidereals and the Nocturnals share, as well as the big things that the Nocturnals have done during the years. I think we should take a step back and tart thinking about any special events which have shaped the Nocturnal culture in the time which has passed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah my take on the Heralds, were just my thoughts on them, mainly to make them seem prominent and for them to fulfill their names as heralds, being the people who start getting the Nocturnals involved in the Times of Tumult. As for your take, my only slight would be the Exalted intentionally placing a curse on their allies to make them obey. Not to my tastes, but that about it. </div> </div> </div>Already ahead of you :P (see the above post. I really think that pledge of loyalty from the side of the Nocturnals could be a good way to integrate the Curse. It may either be an intentional change, like the Solar- Lunar bond, or a result of the Great Curse corrupting the oath of loyalty of the Nocturnals into a cruel joke).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T09:16:40-07:00","id":1320508,"title":"","content":"Iceblade's idea of the Nocturnals exiling themselves into the Firmament gave me an idea for an alternate origin :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever the Night King was, he was but one of many within the Firmament. He ruled over a court of fate-warping half-mad beings just like him, whose whims, if left unchecked, would warp the Firmament, which in turn would introduce fate anomalies into Creation. Their origins are just as unexplained as Nox's own, with some scholars even theorizing that they are all, in fact, different versions of Nox, but no proof exists that would confirm this theory.<br /> <br /> Because every being in this Brotherhood of Night was equally mad and power hungry, none was ever able to rise above his siblings. Realizing he could not rule over his siblings through force, Nox instead created the Harlequins to infiltrate their courts and become their trusted servants, placing his Chosen in a position from which they could shepherd the unwitting beings of Night without them noticing.<br /> <br /> All known records of Nox cease around the time the Nocturnals appeared. It is unclear whether creating the Nocturnals used up all of Nox's power or whether his brothers found out his trickery and exacted revenge, or something else entirely. His plan did work however, as the Harlequins slowly integrated themselves into the chaotic politics of the Firmaments and began stewarding the Night Sky from behind their mask of servitude.<br /> <br /> To this day, most Nocturnals have their hands full keeping the Night Sky in one piece, making their visits upon Creation relatively rare. </div> </div> </div>And here's an idea for the Sidereal Bond :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bond between Sidereal and Nocturnal forms silently over countless starry nights, without the two parties ever actually meeting. A compatibility between their Essence makes it so that Sidereals astrologists sometimes attune themselves to a Nocturnal over many readings and contemplations of the Night Sky, with either side only rarely actually noticing the bond's creation.<br /> <br /> Once bonded, a Nocturnal acts as a Sidereal's guiding star, their Essence of possibilities bringing the Sidereal new insights and greater creativity. At the other end of this bond, the Nocturnal benefits from the patient and orderly Essence of their Sidereal mate, stabilizing their whimsical and chaotic urges when they would lead to terrible consequences.<br /> <br /> Over many incarnations, a Sidereal/Nocturnal pair gains a sense of familiarity with this strange bond, cultivating the sense that someone out there is looking out for them even though they rarely if ever meet each other. The first meeting of a Sidereal/Nocturnal pair is said to be an especially transcendent experience, as though they had finally found a person they had been looking for not only their whole life but in fact for several lifetimes. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T10:33:13-07:00","id":1320526,"title":"","content":"So let's break apart what we have about the history of the Nocturnals-<br /> <br /> - The Divine Revolution, the gods win, out of honor and respect the Nocturnal Host which has supported the gods pledge loyalty to them, and with that their Essence twists and shifts into forming the Curse of Subservience. The Nocturnals which have fought against the gods, however, are judged to death by the Solars. I suggest that the Nocturnals which served the gods beg for mercy for their siblings, and the Sidereals which convinced the rest of the Exalted to choose choose exile over execution- for the war was bloody enough without forcing the Nocturnals to see their kin dies. As a result, the rogue Nocturnals are banished beyond the Gates of Night and into the Firmament. That was when the division between the Heralds and the Harlequins was formed.<br /> <br /> - Through the First Age, the Nocturnals worked in the background of the rest of the Host, using their talents in order to magnify and support the Exalts, just like the sky contain and serves as the background for the luminaries which shine through it. Due to the pledge, the Nocturnals have became servants of the courts of the Exalted- but never slaves, as they chose their own masters and helped them to show what possibilities the future had for them, and how great their light could shine. Some Nocturnals may have even made small kingdoms around them, becoming guardian spirits for whole nations as they worked to bring fourth the future only they could see. Dropping some names for the miracles and wonders which the Nocturnals have managed to establish would help to establish the greatness of the Nocturnals in the setting. That should also include details about how the hosts of the Sidereals and the Nocturnals have started to draw closer- as both Exalted have worked to shape the future, both from without (the Sidereals) and from within (Nocturnals). It should also include a number of events where the two hosts worked together and what they have achieved. Also, this section should name drop instances when the Nocturnals went against the wished of the Old Realm due to their unexpected nature.<br /> <br /> - The coming of the Usurpation. Instead of them predicting what is going to come due to &quot;observing the behaviors&quot; of the Solars, I would instead move it to be completely the result of their ties with the Sidereals. As the Harlequins are compelled to serve, we should also note that as the light of the First Age has started to fall and the Solars fell victim to their hubris, the Nocturnals were enforced to constantly fight over control against their mad patrons- twisting their own words against them and showing them not the future that they wanted, but the future that they needed, as a warning. When the Usurpation has been decided, the Sidereals have tried to keep the Nocturnals in the dark as they knew that if they couldn't decide between two possibilities, adding the endless possibilities that the Nocturnals saw in their dreams would not help. When the Bronze Faction assassinated the Gold Faction, the Nocturnals were their next targets- yet many of the Sidereals could break the bond and warned their bound partners to hide their presence. As the Nocturnal Host debated what to do, many have been is favor of finding escape beyond the Gates of Night, even though some have decided to stay by the side of their patrons- even if it meant to die beside them. As such, in the darkest night when even the stars didn't shine, the Nocturnals broke the seal upon the Gates of Night and left for the Firmament.<br /> <br /> - the time period known as the Exodus, when the Nocturnals of the Firmament have stumbled upon the strange civilizations of mutated humans and other beings which live beyond the Gates of Night. There, they have started to establish their own civilizations and cultures, build around the Caelian City. In the Firmament, they discovered desolated palaces and abandoned temples, all seem to have been built by the Heralds of ages past yet their creators were nowhere to be found. Fighting against the strange denizens of the Firmament and being so close to the touch of Nox for the first time, the Harlequins had to find a place of their own upon the desolated heaven- some have became jesters and servants of the so called &quot;lords of the Firmament&quot;, twisting their wishes and turning them into puppet rulers, or perhaps even serving them truthfully just as they did in the First Age. On the same time, those Harlequins which have stayed in Creation had their own issues to deal with- being reincarnated all alone in the wilderness, the Sidereals have kept a close watch to try and find signs for new Nocturnals in order to guide them and make sure they would stay out of the way- or, if they were not willing to listen, to brand them as Anathema and send the Wyld Hunt after them. Mentioning a few cool things they could have done during this time could be awesome. The Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade, of course, would destroy anything of value which the Nocturnals have made in Creation, and the beginning of the Realm would change everything.<br /> <br /> - During the rise of the Realm, the Nocturnals have established their own civilization upon the Firmament. Caelian City became the center of their culture, the only place where there were no masters and no servants. But around the Firmament, they served the local powers and brought them into greatness, while fighting the strange terrors which lurked beyond the Gates of Night. Around this time, they have started once more to maintain contact with their siblings in Creation, and discovered the harsh condition they had to deal with. Working together, the Nocturnals have started to tighten their relationship with Creation, reaching beyond the Gates of Night to introduce a new future to those who had no hope, and find possibilities in the heart of despair. As whole, the Nocturnals have tried to stay neutral in the Lunar- Realm conflict, but a few always found themselves being drawn to one of the sides, offering their talents under cover in order to bring fourth the future those people dreamed of. Meanwhile a few Nocturnals have even found themselves in Yu Shan, following the millennia old bond and try and help Heaven to see there is another future than the one they saw- yet the Bronze Faction has grew suspicious toward their companions, and only a few Nocturnals have returned to serve among them. Once and awhile, a Nocturnal may even throw their lot with a new Exalted Solar, but the Wyld Hunt have usually put an end to such companionship.<br /> <br /> - the Time of Tumult has began. A new Solar warlord, the Bull of the North, brought ruin upon the Realm. The Empress is gone, and no one knows to where she went. A civil war is brewing in the Imperial City, while the Lunars bar their fangs against their ancient enemies. A corpse mountain rose upon Thorns, bringing the dead from the Underworld. The Solars returned, and with them came their dark reflections- the strange Abyssals with all of their macabre glory. Ancient Sidereal has declared a war against Heaven, and brought with him strange Exalted- ones which are both familiar and strange to the Nocturnals, in many ways like kin and in others... something else. The status que has been breached, and Nox's laughter rings all across the Firmament and whispers in the minds of his Chosen. As the Harlequins debate what to do, strange entities come to the Firmament, claiming their ancient thrones and gathering their armies against Caelian City and Creation alike. The Heralds have returned, and with them a single message- join us to bring a future free from masters, or die among those you chose to serve.<br /> <br /> The future seems gloom- but who if not the Night's Chosen could find a new possibility which no one could expect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T10:43:16-07:00","id":1320528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320508#post1320508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iceblade's idea of the Nocturnals exiling themselves into the Firmament gave me an idea for an alternate origin :<br /> <br /> And here's an idea for the Sidereal Bond :</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't really think I like that origin? I mean, it kinda feels too much like an inversion of 2e's presentation of Luna and her aspects, and it really limits the Nocturnals into operating in the Firmament and maintaining order in it, which is kind of too much like what the Alchemical are doing in their own, isolated world. I personally prefer the Nocturnals to be more involved in Creation, especially as the developers has said explicitly a number of times that Creation is big enough that something like the Nocturnals could easily exist in it without disturbing the setting. It is just not really my cup of tea, I must admit.<br /> <br /> I do like the way you present the Sidereal/ Nocturnal bond. It being a result of personal connection between the fate of one and the dreams of another does makes it interesting, especially since with the bond being personal and created over time it would make a good difference to the reincarnated bond which is exists between the Solars and the Lunars. The reason for why the bond exist still should be explored- instead of saying &quot;it exists because it exists&quot;, there should be a reason for why the two Hosts are connected in such a way,. Perhaps a result of their close work during the First Age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T10:54:07-07:00","id":1320531,"title":"","content":"So has anyone ever thought of at least just including the concept of Kulpa's (the idea of a Multiverse) to Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T11:06:20-07:00","id":1320533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320531#post1320531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So has anyone ever thought of at least just including the concept of Kulpa's (the idea of a Multiverse) to Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is definitely on my to-do list, as the concept of many-worlds is one of the core themes of Nocturnals. The execution is still being thought upon, as we wish to integrate it in a way which would fit 3e the best way possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T11:12:25-07:00","id":1320537,"title":"","content":"Because even if I don't Include Nocturnals I think I would like to Include Kulpa's and the Nocturnals Representation of Nox and his Celestial Barge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T12:51:29-07:00","id":1320558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320528#post1320528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't really think I like that origin? I mean, it kinda feels too much like an inversion of 2e's presentation of Luna and her aspects, and it really limits the Nocturnals into operating in the Firmament and maintaining order in it, which is kind of too much like what the Alchemical are doing in their own, isolated world. I personally prefer the Nocturnals to be more involved in Creation, especially as the developers has said explicitly a number of times that Creation is big enough that something like the Nocturnals could easily exist in it without disturbing the setting. It is just not really my cup of tea, I must admit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. The main idea I was trying to explore was what if Nox created the Nocturnals to be subversive jesters in the first place, rather than them taking up that role as a result of dramatic events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320528#post1320528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the way you present the Sidereal/ Nocturnal bond. It being a result of personal connection between the fate of one and the dreams of another does makes it interesting, especially since with the bond being personal and created over time it would make a good difference to the reincarnated bond which is exists between the Solars and the Lunars. The reason for why the bond exist still should be explored- instead of saying &quot;it exists because it exists&quot;, there should be a reason for why the two Hosts are connected in such a way,. Perhaps a result of their close work during the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. As a funny idea, it could be because the Sidereals spent so much time and energy tracking and trying to predict the Nocturnals, and the Nocturnals spent so much effort trying to steer the Sidereal away from their rigid plans, that at some point it formed a permanent link between the two.<br /> <br /> Maybe in the First Age, the Nocturnals were each assigned a Sidereal to influence while the Sidereal were each assigned a Nocturnal to keep an eye on, with both hosts doing this without telling the other. And whenever it turned out that a Nocturnal had been assigned to influence the same Sidereal who had been tasked with tracking them, a bond would be forged over time. So basically their bond would have originated in a sort playful rivalry rather than with a marriage like with Solars/Lunars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T14:04:18-07:00","id":1320573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320558#post1320558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. The main idea I was trying to explore was what if Nox created the Nocturnals to be subversive jesters in the first place, rather than them taking up that role as a result of dramatic events.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was more or less my initial suggestion, actually- but the split opinions about the Curse of Subservience were the ones which led to it being a result of a certain event which has brought the Curse upon the Nocturnals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That could work. As a funny idea, it could be because the Sidereals spent so much time and energy tracking and trying to predict the Nocturnals, and the Nocturnals spent so much effort trying to steer the Sidereal away from their rigid plans, that at some point it formed a permanent link between the two.<br /> <br /> Maybe in the First Age, the Nocturnals were each assigned a Sidereal to influence while the Sidereal were each assigned a Nocturnal to keep an eye on, with both hosts doing this without telling the other. And whenever it turned out that a Nocturnal had been assigned to influence the same Sidereal who had been tasked with tracking them, a bond would be forged over time. So basically their bond would have originated in a sort playful rivalry rather than with a marriage like with Solars/Lunars </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a cool idea to develop","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T05:08:36-07:00","id":1320718,"title":"","content":"I'd be cautious of having a codified multiverse without getting more of a feel for Getimians.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T08:23:21-07:00","id":1320758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1320718#post1320718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be cautious of having a codified multiverse without getting more of a feel for Getimians.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that makes sense- after all, each Getimian is originated from an alternative timeline, if not outright containing it.<br /> <br /> I actually thought about leaving the details for how such worldines form a mystery, and simply have places in the Firmament which allow access to them and be satisfied with that. I assume that some people may want a more in-depth look in those, but my plan was that while the Nocturnals know where to find those &quot;convergence spots&quot; and whole concepts around them, in the end, they don't really understand them. Still, better to wait for Getimians before we enter too deep into that subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T14:46:10-07:00","id":1321259,"title":"","content":"So while we work conceptually on the history section, let's talk about the Exaltation process-<br /> <br /> We first need to consider the moment of Exaltation. Currently, we have three examples for such moments, and a few details about others. Each Exaltation seems to have some kind of a trend, even though it is not always consistent- Solar Exaltation usually ignites in righteous people, Luna usually choose among the ranks of survivors and potential heroes, the blood of the Dragons is needed to spark their elemental images, but is not guarantee. Sidereal Exaltation is fated, Abyssal Exaltation is a choice, Liminal Exaltation is made.. there are many trends about how and why someone would Exalt, but there are always exceptions. Sometimes, the patron visits the newly Chosen. In others, they stay mute, aloof or uncaring. All according to the principles and themes of the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> In 2e, the Nocturnal Exaltation is based around those which had thwart fates. As 3e refuse to set harsh rules and gives only trends, we can play with it to define that Nocturnals are usually chosen from those which had a possibility in their life- it usually comes with a strong desire which seems to never be fulfilled. An impossible love, impossible hate- the future Nocturnal wish, yearns, needs to break out of the circumstances they live in, and find a way out. They break out from starry strings, and dive deep into the abyss which lurks between them. A territory is endless possibilities.<br /> <br /> Nox, after all, is an entity of two main aspects- possibility, and desire. Usually, such traits show up in times of dire stress or despair- but not always. Nocturnal Exaltation may bless anyone who wants something more than life itself. Even the riches of Dynasts discover that money can't but everything, and even the happiest person may have regrets. Not every wish goes fulfilled, however- and the strength of the desire does not necessarily dictates the chances for Exaltation. An ages long unrequited love may go unnoticed by the eyes of the Midnight King, but a short moment of envy when you discover your old friend married your childhood crush could open the world for a new possibility. Nox is a jester, after all- and his nature is to defy expectation.<br /> <br /> Similarly to their Sidereal cousins, the Nocturnal Exaltation is somewhat a Mystery Play- even if a bit more theatrical than the path of omens the former walk. Nocturnal Exaltation is not a short moment of spiritual awakening- it is a process, even though that the time for it is far from constant. Sometimes, the future Nocturnals seems to be raving like a madman for days or weeks, talking to people only they can see and interact with invisible objects and entities. Sometimes, it is as short as an heartbeat- but in the mind of the Chosen, whole life has passed. Time perception twists and turns as the Play goes on, presenting a vision only the Nocturnal could see. During the Exaltation, the would be Nocturnal follows a strange path- a way to the world where their desire is fulfilled. It is not an alternative world- it does not promise to change the past, but it does shows them the future. I shows them a path- not the only path, but one possible path- where their passion could be fulfilled. The path is personal one- and a dangerous one. Nox is a trickster god- and those who get lost in their heart may never find the way back.<br /> <br /> Not all Nocturnals find what they wish for in the end of the path- sometimes, they willingly let go of their desire, understanding that it is only one single possibility the future has to offer. Sometimes, they discover that what they wished for is not what they wanted, and that they may have the tools to discover their true passion, their true desire. And sometimes, the Nocturnals indeed discover the way for their true bliss, the path they need to walk to fulfill their greatest wish. Those Nocturnals are the least fortunate (at least, among those who manage to find the way out)- for when they open their eyes, they discover that all that they saw was merely a dream, an illusion, a whisper of a mad god in the depths of their mind, and that the world they live in is just as corrupted and fallen as it always been. But it could be different. There is another possibility.<br /> <br /> The mad god whispers- and his Chosen listens.<br /> <br /> The question is, in that case, where is Nox? Unlike the shining Sun or the changing Luna, Nox does not reveal himself in the Mystery Play- but he is there. He is everywhere. Every person you talk with, with object you touch, every scent you smell or song you hear- it's Nox. Sometimes, those marked by the Empyrean have a greater interaction with the God of Night, hearing his voice whispering to them, guiding them, leading them to their path. But those whispers are just as misguiding as helping- for Nox does not take sides, and does not choose favorites. Everyone are equal before the Midnight King, the Indigo Jester gives all a fair chance. However, there is at least one sign of contact between the Onyx Youth and his Chosen- when the Mystery Play reach its conclusion, who the Nocturnal could have been turns to look at who the Nocturnal is. Rarely they pronounce a sentence, a word- again, especially if the Chosen is among the Empyreans or, sometimes, the Nebulas. Usually, they just laugh in their face.<br /> <br /> That's when the Play is over- but the real show just begins.<br /> <br /> Cloaked with dark majesty, the Nocturnals are marked by six signs, Caste Marks which corresponds to the strange and unexplained phenomena which lurks between the stars- Novas, Comets and Auroras are the illuminating phenomena, Empyrean, Nebula and Singularity are the dark ones. It should be noted that those names may be changed in the future, such as if some of the new Exalts would correspond to phenomena such as auroras or comets. Meanwhile, we'll retain those Caste names- as well as their roles. Troubadours, Gladiators, Ambassadors, Jesters, Magicians and Philosophers. Those roles define them and their relationships with their chosen masters- how they serve, and how they'll achieve their dream while serving.<br /> <br /> Once the cold flames of Exaltation cease, the Nocturnal may discover themselves in a different body- not a common occurrence, but it is possible that while walking their own Mystery Play they discovered a body which better fits their desire. The Renewal takes place as Nox's blessing, yet unlike the changing nature of the Lunar Exaltation the change is not reversible, and does not necessarily reflects what the Nocturnal sees as &quot;ideal&quot;- with the future of countless Renewals, alternative identities and potential selves waiting, the current identity is the ones which fits the best for the desire the Nocturnal wish to fulfill. The future is malleable, but once a choice is decided, it should be committed to the very end.<br /> <br /> Like all Exalts, the Nocturnals feel the rush of Essence Fever, driving them into greatness- but unlike others, the Nocturnals discover that their fire is quenched, bound, tamed. Thousand years old loyalty pledge has left its mark upon the Essence of the Nocturnals, and as the dying words of the fallen titans fell upon their murderers, it turned the words of the Nocturnals into chains. They are still driven to do great and terrible things- but all in the name of others, all in the name of those they hold dear, all in the name of their love and hate. Their passion binds them, and the stronger the desire the stronger the binds become. They find themselves compelled to serve, to support, to set the stage for their heroes to shine while they stand in the darkness and watch as they grant the future others wish for. Yet their service is not without a price- words bound their loyalty, and words hold sway upon them, but those are the words alone. Be careful what you wish from a Nocturnal servant- they may very well grant it to you more than you beyond you could have ever imagined.<br /> <br /> Trickery and servitude clash among the Harlequins- the future they wish vs the one their patrons wish, their desires against themselves, twisting the words of those whom they love and hate in order to find freedom inside them. The Heralds, however, are different. Those who fought together with the ancients have still suffered their wrath- for the dying curse could not distinguish between a friend and a foe. Or perhaps, it did- and the madness of the Heralds is all natural to their chaotic visions. Who knows? Still, the Heralds find their Essence burning strongly, its chill flames itch and burn and devour all which should have bound them to the world. Freedom, self indulgence, desire- the Herald is the center of their own universe, and all of the world's light is contained within their dark cloaks. The passions of the Heralds leads them to call upon the future only they can see- and those which try to stop that future should have no place in it.<br /> <br /> Bound or free, all Nocturnals share a core trait- the ability to call upon the darkness and conjure miracles into the world. Fluctuations twist and turn the threads of fate as they draw upon a possibility which does not yet exist, but could be. Potential futures are born from the yearning minds of the Night's Chosen, and the darkness shapes the make their wishes true. Yet each of those Fluctuations is merely a temporary miracle- it does not fulfill the future, it simply makes one such possibility true enough, that even the world itself forgets it is just a possibility. Patrons of the Harlequins may demand impossible demands from the Nocturnals- and the Night's Chosen would happily grant them their wishes in the form of a false and temporary world. No matter how harsh the situation is, the Nocturnals know that they can look into the night's sky and search after a different possibility- and when they make a wish upon the night, their wishes always, always come true, and the world would change to make their dreams fulfilled.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, that's what I have in mind. Feel free to criticize and say what you think about it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T15:06:43-07:00","id":1321264,"title":"","content":"I like it. One thing about the trigger for Exaltation though - I figure what the person wants more than life should be something that's actually possible to achieve. After all, if what they want is impossible it would be a bit hard to show them a possible future where it actually happens. Plus this would avoid the situation where someone who wants to resurrect the dead more than life would fulfill the criteria for both a Nocturnal and a Liminal Exaltation at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T15:19:46-07:00","id":1321267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1321264#post1321264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. One thing about the trigger for Exaltation though - I figure what the person wants more than life should be something that's actually possible to achieve. After all, if what they want is impossible it would be a bit hard to show them a possible future where it actually happens. Plus this would avoid the situation where someone who wants to resurrect the dead more than life would fulfill the criteria for both a Nocturnal and a Liminal Exaltation at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was definitely my intention- hence why I said that it can only show a future, not change the past. I forgot that the other &quot;Big No&quot; together with time travel is reviving the dead. So yeah, the Exaltation would show a possibility where the desire which drew Nox's attention is granted- but the Nocturnal may discover that what is possible may not be what they wanted.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the future has to be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T17:18:10-07:00","id":1321283,"title":"","content":"it looks pretty fine to me. For the Castes I would think it would be okay to keep them all. Of the patrons unknown. The only ones I can see maybe being trouble is Getimian's and Hearteaters. Hearteaters anima being to suspiciously to much like an Aurora. But I think thats fine, they are optional. Being as canon as Nocturnals. If you would want to include both in a game, then it would be simple enough to say that their is no Aurora Caste and then just round it out with Singularity replacing them. If not then you can include them both. I think that while Nocturnals should be informed of the optionals design-wise their is no need to acknowledge them unless you want to in individual games. So the only worry is Getimians, since we have no idea what their patron is like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T00:43:46-07:00","id":1321356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1321283#post1321283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it looks pretty fine to me. For the Castes I would think it would be okay to keep them all. Of the patrons unknown. The only ones I can see maybe being trouble is Getimian's and Hearteaters. Hearteaters anima being to suspiciously to much like an Aurora. But I think thats fine, they are optional. Being as canon as Nocturnals. If you would want to include both in a game, then it would be simple enough to say that their is no Aurora Caste and then just round it out with Singularity replacing them. If not then you can include them both. I think that while Nocturnals should be informed of the optionals design-wise their is no need to acknowledge them unless you want to in individual games. So the only worry is Getimians, since we have no idea what their patron is like</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we will be a lot smarter after we'll get the Storyteller's Companion and Exigents, but meanwhile, we'll work with what we have..<br /> <br /> I'll soon make a Google Drive so we could work on each chapter individually, and I'll put what we have for the first chapter in there. My tendency for now it developing the project chapter after chapter, while keep brainstorming upon the future ones in the process. If someone else has a different approach to the development process, or is inspired to work on some other chapter, I'm open for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T02:06:49-07:00","id":1321993,"title":"","content":"So I've finished writing the first draft for the history section. It got a bit longer than a page and a half, so we may need to edit it a bit to reduce the wordcount (I think that 5 pages is the budget for the first chapter, and while we don't have to follow the same rigid frame as the canon books, have such limitations would help us to focus on the subject, and I do have the tendency to use flowery language for no real reason :P).<br /> <br /> Anyway, you can find it here-<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BulKhy44ENvj8xgQOSqZDWCpkPXgj0MvXxC0_5qXclA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">View link</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eDGeFy-lzBLjKk9xxoDc0R85GWMW8sqC8BlC1x770JE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">comment link</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T12:07:29-08:00","id":1353081,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say I like a lot of what you guys had been coming up with here. In particular, I like the inversion of Heralds and Harlequins regarding the Curse of Subservience. I'd rebrand that as an Oath of Allegiance, which would play off a Major or Defining Tie of Loyalty to some individual or group that the Harlequin serves - it might not longer be targeted specifically at other Exalts anymore, though it could if that's who the Harlequin is feeling loyal to. <br /> <br /> I also like introducing them to the setting earlier. Many of the choices I made for the Nocturnals originally were the result of needing to jump through an increasing number of hoops to plug them into 2E. It seems to me that 3E is more flexible in that regard. Plenty of new types of Exalts just out there wandering the world in some fashion. <br /> <br /> If they all retreated to the Caelian City, I think an explanation would be needed to explain why they've remained there. Are all the Nocturnals centuries old at this point and no new ones have exalted in Creation since they departed? Is something about the City confining their exaltations there? Are the Nocturnal Elders abducting younger Nocturnals whenever they exalt? <br /> <br /> Speaking of abduction, I noticed that putting the Nocturnals in a space city kind of makes them the Aliens to the Sidereal's MIB. I wonder if something could be done by steering into that comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T12:31:50-08:00","id":1353097,"title":"","content":"Thanks for replying, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2118_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2118\" data-vbnamecard=\"2118\">Reminiscent Oasis</a>! As the original creator of the Nocturnals, having your approval on some of the ideas in here is very important to me. I must say I do like the concept of elder Nocturnals reaching &quot;beyond space&quot; and abducting some of their recently Exalted kin &quot;for their own protection&quot;. I hope to return and finish this project, but doing such a thing alone is a bit difficult. I hope that by the time that Exigents would show up, I'll already find the mental resources to finish, at the very least, most of the fluff and setting about Nocturnals in 3e (as I plan on waiting for this book until I'll start with the mechanics, not to mention that anything related to multiple timelines is on hold until we'll know more about Getimians).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T12:45:34-08:00","id":1353102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1353097#post1353097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope to return and finish this project, but doing such a thing alone is a bit difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me about it!<br /> <br /> I'm still on the fence about whether I'd want to pursue the Nocturnals in 3E. For me it comes down to seeing what the Getimians are up to.<br /> <br /> On the bright side though, the Heart-eaters sound a lot like the old Apocalyptic Exalted I never got around to writing for 2E. Maybe I'll do those as a fan version of Heart-Eaters since we probably won't see them until 2025 if we're lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T13:16:41-08:00","id":1353120,"title":"","content":"Hearteaters are going to be featured in Exigents next year.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T13:22:46-08:00","id":1353123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1353120#post1353120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hearteaters are going to be featured in Exigents next year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooner than I expected. Are Heartearters a type of Exigent, or are Exigents, Hearteaters, Getimians, Umbrals, etc., getting put in the same book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T13:25:27-08:00","id":1353128,"title":"","content":"All three optional ones are not Exigents, but their own (optionally canon) splat you can make by using Exigent rules (which are pretty much also rules for making other splats and whatnot) Getimians are not going to be in Exigents, those are an actual canon splat. The ones in Exigents are Hearteaters, Dream-Souled and Umbral Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T18:38:27-08:00","id":1353198,"title":"","content":"Where can I read this info? I think I backed everything, did I miss this update?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T20:54:02-08:00","id":1353237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1353198#post1353198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I read this info? I think I backed everything, did I miss this update?</div> </div> </div> </div>9/10 they slip details like this into the Monday Meeting blog or the pathcast. Explictly about the contents of Exigents, the question came up multiple times and we got some answers in the Ask the Devs thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T07:19:41-08:00","id":1353344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318724-at-the-throne-of-chaos-nocturnal-3e-brainstorming-thoughts?p=1353123#post1353123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooner than I expected. Are Heartearters a type of Exigent, or are Exigents, Hearteaters, Getimians, Umbrals, etc., getting put in the same book?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned. Hearteaters, Dreamsouled and Umbrals are optional canon and featured in the Exigents book as further options of possible Exalt types.<br /> Apparently the new team apparently had some misgivings about how so many new Exalt types had been promised (certainly the shedule made it look laughably unrealistic) but at the same time the core did kind of promise 3 more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}